{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it","id":596106,"title":"Fixing Beast: how would you have done it?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-19T14:57:59-07:00","id":596106,"title":"Fixing Beast: how would you have done it?","content":"The Beast controversy has been ongoing on these forums - and the RPG.net forums, from what little I know - for a while. The initial draft release attracted lots of debate, the official rewrite attracted even more.<br /> <br /> But I was wondering: for those of you who had problems with Beast, either before or after the revamp, how would you have fixed them?<br /> <br /> Myself? Well, I haven't been able to memorise the thread here, nevermind the RPG.net equivalent, but still...<br /> <br /> #1: Horrors wrapped in human flesh<br /> One of the things I liked about draft!Beast was the presentation of Beasts as literally born monsters. This is something touched on only be three other splats in the NWoD; Werewolves, Prometheans and Demons. Of those three, werewolves are often conflicted about whether or not they are happier now, demons have to feign humanity as best they can to survive, and the whole point of prometheans is to become human. Beasts, as they were presented, were something unique: monsters from birth who were actually happier when they accepted the truth.<br /> <br /> &quot;I am a monster who dreamed he was a man. But the dream is over. And the monster is awake.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's not something integral to the other lines. It was in Beast, and that was a perspective I liked for its uniqueness. I don't mind using the term &quot;Horror&quot; to refer to a Beast's inner self, because that actually a good emphasis of the theme; humans have souls, but Beasts are horrors wearing a human suit. However, the term &quot;Homecoming&quot; is essential to me; it emphasizes that a Beast is closer to a Mage or a Werewolf than to a Vampire or a Changeling. No exterior agency acted on them to make them into a Beast; it was just who they always were, and they finally accepted it.<br /> <br /> <br /> #2: Eat to live, don't live to eat<br /> Beasts need to feed. That's just how it is. Everything needs sustenance. Beasts just happen to feed on fear and horror. Something all Beasts must learn to live with is that, no matter what humans think, they are still nothing more than meat, singing to itself in the darkness. But that doesn't mean a Beast shouldn't exercise restraint. A Beast must learn how to balance its hunger with the world around them; do they try to be humane and feed &quot;reasonably&quot;, or do they embrace their dark side and gorge themselves, heedless of the destruction they cause?<br /> <br /> It's alright for Beasts to want to put a higher meaning on why they feed or how they feed, but as more than one complainer has noted, the revision's &quot;Beasts terrify humanity to teach lessons&quot; comes off as foolish and pretentious. At best, it's worth a social Z-axis foundation, but I don't think it's strong enough to be the underlying purpose of the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> #3: Heroes only in their own mind<br /> The biggest problem with draft!Beast was the very use of the term &quot;Heroes&quot; in my opinion. No matter the higher cause behind it, the basic fact is that people associate &quot;hero&quot; with &quot;good guy&quot; - it's our cultural indoctrination. And if the other side are the Heroes, then, by simple logic, we Beasts <b>must</b> be the Villains. This simple fact, more than anything, incited readers to sympathize with the Heroes and look more harshly upon the Beasts.<br /> <br /> Personally, I would call such people &quot;Slayers&quot;. It's a much less loaded term that emphasizes who and what they are: they are Killers of Beasts. Morality has nothing to do with it, except maybe as the excuse they use when called upon it. They just want to kill Beasts. That's all that matters to them.<br /> <br /> <br /> #4: Slayers are born, not made<br /> The other big problem with Heroes, from my perspective, is that they were given a mechanical creation basis. This fueled the sympathetic interpretation of them and caused the schism between Hero supporters and Beast supporters.<br /> <br /> I say that if a mortal rises up against a Beast because of that Beast's depredations, that's a Hunter, more tahn anything else. It's the universal thread that underlies all supernatural splats in the NWoD: Actions Have Consequences. Bully mortals too much, and humans will fight back. It's simple Cause and Effect.<br /> <br /> I think Slayers should just arise. There's no need for malignancy on a Beast's part. A Slayer-to-be sees a Beast, and she <b>knows</b> that they are a monster. The Beast does nothing to them; she could just be passing by in the street, buying a coffee and a donut at a local stall, sitting on the bus, and it still doesn't matter. When a Slayer sees a Beast, they undergo their own twisted version of the Homecoming, finally realizing their place in life.<br /> <br /> In fact, ideally, I think a Slayer potential should be immune to the Feasting of a hungry Horror. This would emphasize how shallow and selfish their goals are. They don't suffer from the Beast's presence, they don't experience anything to push them into accepting their role, they just open their arms and embrace it, as willingly as a Beast does.<br /> <br /> <br /> These are the things I think of when I consider what I would have done to make Beast the best I think it could be. How would you have fixed whatever problems you see or saw in Beast?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T15:29:14-07:00","id":596212,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I found both of the drafts to be relatively good. Not as good as the other 2nd ed games but good nonetheless. The core idea of Beast is unique. I'm not certain that I'd change the things you've mentioned too much. I'd just like the existing material to be expanded a bit more. I do think the lesson teaching should be more egotistical (think Smaug) rather than &quot;wisdom&quot;, but that's hardly a deal-breaker.<br /> <br /> The notion of Family and the cross-over parts of the game are the most underdeveloped (indeed in some places they almost make the game into the Care Bears cartoon), so I'm hoping that the final draft fleshes them out more. Likewise the spirit rules were simply copy and pasted into the drafts without any meaningful reason for being there. I'm hoping that the final draft replaces them with a &quot;spirit&quot; section that is better aligned to the game's themes. Expanding on astral / primordial dream denizens would seem appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T16:24:10-07:00","id":596262,"title":"","content":"I like most of the stuff in the revision.<br /> <br /> It's just, the Beast Cultural Focus and the Homecoming being replaced with the Devouring are both awful.<br /> <br /> I'm bolding my actual fixes, so if you dont ant to read a rant, skip to the bold<br /> <br /> I continue to insist that &quot;Scare or hurt mortals to teach them lessons&quot; is a horribly position for the culture of an entire splat. All of the complaining about Beasts being abusive assholes becomes more valid in that context. Furthermore, it's far too restricting when it comes to character concepts.<br /> <br /> If an entire culture is based around teaching mortals lessons, then a Beast who does not teach mortals lessons is going to be looked down on by other Beasts. So, if you dont want to be a beast that teaches lessons, then you're automatically an outcast from society.<br /> <br /> I now will note that New Beasts cultural thematic is most similar to the Lancea et Sanctum(scare mortals and punish sin, for as the children of Longinus, we are the monsters that scare humanity back into the embrace of YHWH/Jehovah/Christ/Allah/Other Name for Abrahamic God or Similar being) and the Scarecrow Ministry(Scare the fuck out of mortals with Hoaxes so that they'll either stay the hell away from this gate to the hedge or be too busy investigating the hoax to do something about it) Both of which are sub splats.<br /> <br /> <b>If I understand correctly, this focus was added so that Beasts would have more to do on their own, instead of in crossover games.<br /> <br /> I say that that could have been accomplished by say, something similar to the dread power &quot;build a monster&quot; rules from hunter. an Appendix of unique critters with ties to the Dark Mother for beasts to investigate.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, The Presence of Z-Splats could have provided that focus, in which case &quot;Scare the hell out of humans to teach them a lesson&quot; would fit better there, among other options</b><br /> <br /> The Devouring has all kinds of problems.<br /> <br /> Before, a nascent beast was always a monster, and by coming home she discovered her true family.<br /> <br /> Now, it's a person who had a sleep disorder has their soul hollowed out and a monster climb inside so that they can get super powers and join a club.<br /> <br /> That's... Not the game we were promised. We were promised a game about family. This is not family.<br /> <br /> When you're born human and become a monster, then you do not belong to the first race of monsters. You're not the primordial progenitor, you're the upstart mortal who's apping everybody elses shit, then claiming that makes you their big brother..<br /> <br /> In addition to this, the fact that you now become a beast because another Beast ate your soul to make room for your Horror is... Supposedly it's to give the character more agency, except. &quot;You one day realize that the monster in your nightmare is and always was you&quot; is much more agency than &quot;some other guy decided to invite you to the club and offered you a choice to join... except sometimes he coerces you or just eats your soul without telling you what's going on.&quot;<br /> <br /> The first is something you do, the second is something someone else does. Net loss in agency.<br /> <br /> And it's really inconsistent with the fiction, and is just jarring when you look at all of the &quot;Family&quot; stuff.<br /> <br /> Also, anyone who willfully joins a culture where super powered individuals use violence or scare tactics to force their own views on morality or teach &quot;lessons&quot; to mortals is probably an asshole. Even if he only hurts their assholes, he's still an asshole.<br /> <br /> Now, there's the sidebar on homecomings instead of devourings, but it's inconsistent with how the devouring is depicted and really feels most like a half assed appeasement than an actual address at the potential complaint.<br /> <br /> <b>If I understand correctly, this major change was made to justify a scenario in which an elder beast is there to provide and introduction on Beast culture...Except, that could have been done much more easily with a &quot;Beasts can tell when a nascent sibling is about to undergo their homecoming&quot; power, and a mention that some older beasts tend to get maternal or paternal feelings about younger beasts and tend to approach them to help them adjust to realizing what they really are.<br /> <br /> Everything else about the revisions, the changes to heroes, the rewritten stereotypes, and the one family's new boon, all of that's good, keep that.</b><br /> <br /> It's just, two major unnecessary changes kind of ruin the game we were promised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T11:32:30-07:00","id":597093,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">While hacks and alternative takes on gamelines are welcome on these forums, we do not need another thread retooling the same old complaints about beast. We've got enough of those already. If this thread careens into the same misanthropy the mod team will shut it down.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T11:49:14-07:00","id":597112,"title":"","content":"I think the best idea I ever saw about fixing Beast was that Heroes create Beasts. Somebody feels an overwhelming need to be a hero for one reason or another, so they point to somebody and say &quot;look he's a Beast, I shall slay him&quot;.<br /> <br /> You play that somebody trying to cope with a world that sees you as a monster for frankly stupid reason and hails the bigot trying to lynch you.<br /> <br /> Oh, and I'd make the sample Heroes one republican who goes after democrats. One democrat who goes after republicans. And one crazy guy who's convinced the government is full of lizard men. I'm off the opinion that distancing a game from whatever it's metaphorically about helps people look at things from a new angle - and also that it's just plain interesting to explore an idea from different angels than you might actually see in the real world. Pro-George III monarchists as America's hated scapegoat? Why not.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd also have done a lot more with Chambers. The Lair is the coolest part of Beast IMO, so making where and why you choose each and every last Chamber have mechanical and story repercussions would be cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T13:21:58-07:00","id":597200,"title":"","content":"I think that all in all, Beast is a good game and does not needs to be &quot;fixed&quot;. Sure, there are some thing I liked better in the first draft (like the Homecoming instead of Devouring and Souls instead of Horrors) and some thing I liked better in the second draft (the &quot;look from without&quot; sidebars people or the change in the Hero's role) and some things which I'm still not sure about (like the whole &quot;teaching humanity the lessons of the Dark Mother&quot;)- but I like the game. For me, &quot;fixing&quot; the game would be more of mix and match of the two drafts.<br /> <br /> Also, I think that not calling Heroes &quot;Heroes&quot; or making Beasts the response to their enemies instead of the other way around would kinda ruin the theme of the game. From the way I see it, the fact that you need to make the process of using the word &quot;Hero&quot; as the antagonist instead of the protagonist, and the fact that the power behind the story is the Beast and the Hero is just a secondary character in its myth is what makes the game so different from the others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T14:23:51-07:00","id":597317,"title":"","content":"I've never understood people wanting to change it so Heroes are called Slayers. I mean Hero fits the mindset of slay the monster, save the day and then be rewarded with praise, accolades, wealth, and unlimited rice pudding.It also informs on what they think of themselves that they are the Heroes. If you call them Slayers you're just saying they kill things which doesn't really evoke anything beyond it, Slayers anime/manga/light novel series aside, and it kind of makes you wonder what the point of them is as opposed to just having the nemesis be Hunters or Slashers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T15:10:02-07:00","id":597365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=597317#post597317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never understood people wanting to change it so Heroes are called Slayers. I mean Hero fits the mindset of slay the monster, save the day and then be rewarded with praise, accolades, wealth, and unlimited rice pudding.It also informs on what they think of themselves that they are the Heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the term Hero was being used ironically. At least in the first edition, where they didn't save the day and were't rewarded and only killed out of a twisted need to kill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T19:03:05-07:00","id":597654,"title":"","content":"How about we drop this until the game is <i><b>finished</b></i>? I'm not happy with some of the changes either but that doesn't make them bad. Yes I prefer Homecoming &amp; Soul, rather than Devouring &amp; Horror; that doesn't mean the game needs 'fixing'. What it does mean is that I prefer certain stylistic and thematic elements that have been de-emphasized.<br /> <br /> Whether or not those elements are re-emphasized has yet to be determined. Jumping to conclusions based on the work in progress and our own desires doesn't help. I have no problem with a setting 'hack' or 'shard' being written by the fans to adjust the tone of the game. However that isn't what is happening here and is premature anyway.<br /> <br /> While there has been a good case made for why some people want these changes above the 'common tone' of them, (meaning how the tone of the post can be taken with both the context of this thread and the fewest assumptions based on what is outside of it), is rather...aggressive. Not necessarily hostile but most certainly passionate and determined. Which doesn't appear to be the most tolerant of mindsets. Naturally this is as uncharitable as it is untrue; just because someone cares doesn't mean they can't hear out other views.<br /> <br /> Secondly, it does seem kind of tacky to decry an artist's work when the work has not yet been completed. I admit, that may just be my personal preference but it's not like the Devs don't already know about the issues or have failed to acknowledge them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T20:52:47-07:00","id":597800,"title":"","content":"I think there is a very vocal group who liked the old tone where beasts were beasts. Not evil, not good that was up to how you interacted with the world and heroes spawned naturally to oppose the beasts. The heroes weren't good or evil that much either. While the beast was indeed a nightmare, or fear given form like the fear of retribution, or simple fear of spiders. It didn't matter because the hero figures were no better or worse. Though they are clearly two sides of the same coin. Which I liked myself.<br /> <br /> The Horror/Soul debate I'm neutral on, but over all things are pretty good. I'm not a World of Darkness vet and have only played it one other time and am running a game now with my two NPC's (read ST PC's) Henderson and Knight. These two beasts are pretty fun and honestly I wouldn't mind seeing how they stack up next to other PC beasts. I will agree with Fallen Eco it's too early to decry and call for fixes this isn't the final version of the text and maybe this thread is being read by the developer in which case they may get the idea that some elements we liked better in the first draft. Okay that's fine this isn't the final draft.<br /> <br /> I do like the secondary theme of unintentionally teaching a lesson Red Riding Hood style. So I will give that a big thumbs up but I did also like the term Homecoming. And that you were always the beast, you just didn't realize it. That was an amazing thing and I hope that comes back around. But I think we should all relax a bit and speak calmly. We don't need the WoD boards pouring vitrol like the board I spend most of my time on around here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T21:47:27-07:00","id":597867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=597112#post597112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the best idea I ever saw about fixing Beast was that Heroes create Beasts. Somebody feels an overwhelming need to be a hero for one reason or another, so they point to somebody and say &quot;look he's a Beast, I shall slay him&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sort of runs back into the problem of &quot;well, then it's not a game about family anymore.&quot;<br /> <br /> Not that it isn't cool, but it, to me, at least, seems more like it'd be better as an alternate take from a player's guide.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=597654#post597654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about we drop this until the game is <i><b>finished</b></i>? I'm not happy with some of the changes either but that doesn't make them bad. Yes I prefer Homecoming &amp; Soul, rather than Devouring &amp; Horror; that doesn't mean the game needs 'fixing'. What it does mean is that I prefer certain stylistic and thematic elements that have been de-emphasized.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do believe that the point of releasing the rough drafts for public viewing and use is to get feedback and criticism.<br /> <br /> As long as the criticism is constructive and valid, and arguments don't become heated, there's no reason not to have a thread like this one when things are in flux. Having it when everything is set in stone would just be a huge waste of time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 07-21-2015, 01:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T00:37:12-07:00","id":598032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=597867#post597867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sort of runs back into the problem of &quot;well, then it's not a game about family anymore.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/v/TfmonDIlZ3s?start=90&amp;end=101\" target=\"_blank\">Isn't it?</a> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It's certainly more family than the current Devouring.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T09:13:28-07:00","id":598426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=597365#post597365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the term Hero was being used ironically. At least in the first edition, where they didn't save the day and were't rewarded and only killed out of a twisted need to kill.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought it had something to do with tying the game's themes to the notion of monomyth? <br /> <br /> Honestly both drafts are trying to shoehorn a lot of competing themes in (family vs. monomyth vs fairy tale parables vs cross-over). It's very ambitious to give all of those enough spot-light to feel like they've been done justice. It'll be a pleasant surprise if the final product does at least one of them well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T13:16:48-07:00","id":598643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=598032#post598032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/v/TfmonDIlZ3s?start=90&amp;end=101\" target=\"_blank\">Isn't it?</a> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It's certainly more family than the current Devouring.</div> </div> </div> </div>This I will agree with","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T19:39:25-07:00","id":598948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://pastebin.com/gtAQ7f6A\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://pastebin.com/gtAQ7f6A\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://pastebin.com/gtAQ7f6A\" target=\"_blank\"> http://pastebin.com/gtAQ7f6A </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> There's my answer to the question. It's a work in progress, but the fluff rejiggering is complete. Just gotta work on the mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T21:10:56-07:00","id":599007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=598948#post598948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://pastebin.com/gtAQ7f6A\" target=\"_blank\">http://pastebin.com/gtAQ7f6A</a><br /> <br /> There's my answer to the question. It's a work in progress, but the fluff rejiggering is complete. Just gotta work on the mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, this... this is beautiful, at least to me. It's like a melding of some of the best parts of draft!Beast and the Leviathan fansplat, creating a truly wondrous vision. It could perhaps have absorbed more of the &quot;the other creatures of the night are distant relatives&quot; aspect of official!Beast, but still, this is really good stuff. I can only weep that this isn't the route that OPP decided to go with for their version of the Primordial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T23:25:45-07:00","id":599057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=598948#post598948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://pastebin.com/gtAQ7f6A\" target=\"_blank\">http://pastebin.com/gtAQ7f6A</a><br /> <br /> There's my answer to the question. It's a work in progress, but the fluff rejiggering is complete. Just gotta work on the mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Loving this! Especially the take on heroes. Humanity's immune response gone wild is a splendid direction, baking the classic fall from grace right into the splat. Bravo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T00:39:53-07:00","id":599072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=599007#post599007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, this... this is beautiful, at least to me. It's like a melding of some of the best parts of draft!Beast and the Leviathan fansplat, creating a truly wondrous vision.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's always been both cool and somewhat suprising for me to see how often attempts to fix beast end up taking cues from Leviathan.<br /> <br /> (Well, unless it's a big coincidence)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T05:28:58-07:00","id":599239,"title":"","content":"Only thing I wasn't happy about with Beast was that they didn't have a way to transform into full on monsters in the physical world. When I think of Beast that way, it reminds me of Supernatural or Lost Girl, in which the monsters and mythical creatures look like ordinary humans. The &quot;dragons&quot; in Supernatural were just guys who kidnapped virgins and could burn you with a touch. That's not very appealing to me, it sounds more like a monster flick with a low special effects budget.<br /> <br /> If I could, I would have included a general Atavism dedicated to manifesting the physical traits of the family you're descended from, incurring attribute changes and skill performances that vary by family. At its highest stage of mastery, you fully transform into your monster self! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-22-2015, 08:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T06:39:40-07:00","id":599305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=599072#post599072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's always been both cool and somewhat suprising for me to see how often attempts to fix beast end up taking cues from Leviathan.<br /> <br /> (Well, unless it's a big coincidence)</div> </div> </div> </div>In this case, it is - I've never read Leviathan - but there is that phrase about great minds and fools.<br /> <br /> Also, thanks for the positive feedback, folks! I'll toss up the mechanics here too, once they're done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T07:34:56-07:00","id":599376,"title":"","content":"I think your rewrite is a piece of art, Axel, but in the context of official Beast I see a lot of things that are either apparent in the current draft -- the three births of a Beast are how I already figured a Horror binding itself to a human Soul worked -- or that I'm not a fan of -- Progeny, in this case; I really don't think Beast needs a demisplat.<br /> <br /> I like the Tribes. I might see about stripping out some of the Beast vs. Humans history and seeing how I could port them into a Beast game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T07:45:10-07:00","id":599381,"title":"","content":"Demi-splats are like anything else in these rulebooks, just more tools. Those who don't want to use them don't have to. Like having a nWoD Wraith game doesn't take anything away from fans of oWoD Wraith or nWoD Geist, having demi-splats doesn't take anything away from fans of the main splat. It just gives us more ways to play the game (IMO, a very good thing).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T07:54:32-07:00","id":599400,"title":"","content":"True, more tools is good. I just think the Beast ecosystem is very crowded already, and I'd rather see more space about what mixed broods look like and how Beasts and Kin (or even non-Kin) interact. Also, instead of demibeasts, I'd rather see a Beast-specific revision of the rules for Cryptids or monsters in Mortal Remains. They'd fulfill a similar narrative niche, but wouldn't be as predictable as demibeasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T08:30:42-07:00","id":599439,"title":"","content":"As I like to run dark heroes games, I think I'll use the Beast as antagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T08:43:43-07:00","id":599447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archivist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=599439#post599439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I like to run dark heroes games, I think I'll use the Beast as antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd recommend also including a few Hero (the Beast-hunting kind) antagonists, too. Good contrast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T12:40:23-07:00","id":599700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=599400#post599400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, more tools is good. I just think the Beast ecosystem is very crowded already, and I'd rather see more space about what mixed broods look like and how Beasts and Kin (or even non-Kin) interact. Also, instead of demibeasts, I'd rather see a Beast-specific revision of the rules for Cryptids or monsters in Mortal Remains. They'd fulfill a similar narrative niche, but wouldn't be as predictable as demibeasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is what I'd do with progeny (of the Horror). Unlike the Horror and more like Astral ephemeral beings, these progeny can get out of the lair and into the twilight with all of the usual ephemeral shenanigans that entails. As for demi-splat, IMO a human who has &quot;Kinship&quot; is good enough, better even if their actual relations to the Beast's in some way. But then again, I think the whole Kinship system is a bit to deus ex machina for my tastes and the notions of Family are bit underdeveloped and/or focus on the wrong Family themes. But then I'm also like &quot;more organic story-hooks = better&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T12:57:08-07:00","id":599705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=599700#post599700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this is what I'd do with progeny (of the Horror). Unlike the Horror and more like Astral ephemeral beings, these progeny can get out of the lair and into the twilight with all of the usual ephemeral shenanigans that entails. As for demi-splat, IMO a human who has &quot;Kinship&quot; is good enough, better even if their actual relations to the Beast's in some way. But then again, I think the whole Kinship system is a bit to deus ex machina for my tastes and the notions of Family are bit underdeveloped and/or focus on the wrong Family themes. But then I'm also like &quot;more organic story-hooks = better&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I remember some of your arguments on other threads.<br /> <br /> Having Primordial Dream creatures slipping out and being in Twilight as another class of ephemeral creature would be neat. I might use that idea in a Beast game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T21:00:31-07:00","id":601362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=598032#post598032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's certainly more family than the current Devouring.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so - Devouring creates an immediate bond to another Beast and a family lineage?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T22:50:41-07:00","id":601428,"title":"","content":"Devouring creates family bonds through fictional magic mumbo jumbo. The other Beast doesn't grow up with you or parent you, or anything.<br /> <br /> The Hero creates Beasts model ties them together through shared oppression; tying Beasts metaphorically to the same social factors that led to the habit of African Americans calling each other &quot;brothers&quot; and &quot;sisters&quot;.<br /> <br /> (Technically the Heroes create Beasts system would be a better metaphor for the way anti-semites see Jews than African American oppression. But once you're using supernatural metaphors you're distant enough to draw on both.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T02:00:57-07:00","id":601531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=599239#post599239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only thing I wasn't happy about with Beast was that they didn't have a way to transform into full on monsters in the physical world. When I think of Beast that way, it reminds me of Supernatural or Lost Girl, in which the monsters and mythical creatures look like ordinary humans. The &quot;dragons&quot; in Supernatural were just guys who kidnapped virgins and could burn you with a touch. That's not very appealing to me, it sounds more like a monster flick with a low special effects budget.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreeing with general need for this, but...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=599239#post599239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I could, I would have included a general Atavism dedicated to manifesting the physical traits of the family you're descended from, incurring attribute changes and skill performances that vary by family. At its highest stage of mastery, you fully transform into your monster self! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Does not <b><i>Infestation</i></b> Atvism change you to literall hive of insects with Satiety Expenditure?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BtP, version 1</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Satiety Expenditure: </b>By spending a dot of Satiety, the Beast surrenders to the hive within, and his entire body disintegrates into a mass of insects or spiders, leaving his clothing and worldly possessions behind. In so doing, he becomes a swarm with a radius of two yards per dot of Lair. The area is reduced proportionate to the amount of damage inflicted on him. In other words, the swarm is reduced to half size once half of his Health boxes are filled with damage. The Beast can also condense to attack a single target, inflicting lethal damage each turn equal to his Lair dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T05:56:21-07:00","id":601666,"title":"","content":"True, you do turn into a swarm of insects, but for all we know, their soul could be this giant ant queen and the swarm could be her colony rushing to defend her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T09:16:52-07:00","id":603007,"title":"","content":"I agree with the poster a bit above me, it bothers me too how the Beasts cannot become a monster in the &quot;real&quot; world.<br /> <br /> Beast feels like something that is trying to be about Lovercraftian monsters intruding and bending reality around them. But the way it's currently being portrayed, it feels more like about a furry who claims he's an animal inside and has a lot of werewolf friends. Even the example we got of a Beast feeding while watching a vampire eat felt very awkward - the Beast basically stands there, says &quot;fuck you&quot; to the victim, and does nothing else while the vampire eat - and that's it? It feels more like a groupie who is deluded into thinking he's a supernatural being too than a Cthulu-like monster preying on humanity.<br /> <br /> <br /> If I were to try to &quot;fix&quot; Beast (actually, make it something closer to what I would enjoy), I think the result would be a bit repetitie - it would eventually echo themes from other WoD games - and it would definitely be less cross-over friendly.<br /> <br /> But I would have made it about monsters who are completely alien to our reality, born hidden in human flesh, but still remembering the gigantic, monstrous and impossible beings they truly are. The main themes would be family and trying to find a balance between existing within human flesh and giving in to the monster's unknowable, unspeakable mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2518-erasculio","name":"Erasculio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2518_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T10:12:10-07:00","id":603054,"title":"","content":"From what I'm seeing in the suggestions it seems like people want Beast to be a lot more like the TV show Grimm. I can see how that could work well with regards to physical manifestation of the Beast's soul, though that may get a little too close to Changeling's territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T14:13:48-07:00","id":603186,"title":"","content":"I'll probably houserule a system not unlike a Demon's &quot;Going Loud&quot; mechanic (ironic that I'm borrowing from Demon here), where at the cost of a big hunk of Satiety, you can go full-on monster mode for a while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T14:23:56-07:00","id":603195,"title":"","content":"The word &quot;Atavism&quot;, to me, suggests a certain physicality that, in my mind, works perfectly with the concept that you are a born monster hidden within human flesh. When the teasers started, hearing the word &quot;atavism&quot;, and how Beasts were born monsters made me think of Ferectoi, a special kind of Fomor from the old WtA days. Ferectoi could be as heavily mutated as any Fomor, but all of their mutations were perfectly hidden.<br /> Pretty much all of my players want to be able to transform themselves physically, at least in some ways. One guy only wants to physically manifest Atavisms one or two at a time. A terrifying maw here, fantastic wings there, you know. Gangrel-ish sort of stuff. Another wants to be able to wholly blast out of his skin into the freakish creature he truly is, so that he can run with his werewolf pack and experience the same unity of flesh and spirit that they do.<br /> <br /> edit: I'm also one of those annoying people who thinks that this game could benefit from social splats. Like, teaching Wisdom is cool, and would make for a pretty neat social splat. I also like the crossover-ness of the game, and the theme of Family. I think that a cool way to potentially handle it would be to make each social splat somehow related to how the Beast chooses/interacts with their Family, so ultimately each splat is a different way to approach crossover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","user":"JTroy","date":". 07-25-2015, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T21:29:33-07:00","id":603467,"title":"","content":"Too true, this game seems to me, to put more emphasis on being social with other splats than amongst other beasts.<br /> <br /> Also I'd totally be behind the concept of changing wholly or even partly from the human form to one's true form and run with the other supernaturals. Everyone else can truly show what they are. Werewolves and the Changing Breeds have their different forms, Demons have Going Loud, Changelings have their Mask/Mien, the Bound have the Caul Manifestation, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/24296274/BeastThePrimordial.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","name":"Draca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6566_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T01:33:26-07:00","id":603646,"title":"","content":"you know, what that hooked me into Beast was the fact that they <i>don't</i> change their shape and turn into great dragons and terrible giants out of the blue. Remember the Atavism preview in the Open Blog post? that's what got me- the idea that most people look on beast on the outside and see them do weird things- but they can't see who they are. From the outside, they are just people with strange power. Those who are family, however, can see the shadows and echos of the true Beast's Soul/Horror, and the closer they are the more they see.<br /> <br /> I can't really say why I find it so appealing- but the idea of people who look half crazy and are covered by the thought of who they think they are just feels awesome from the way I see it. It both reinforce the &quot;family&quot; theme and the horror of the game, where simple shapeshifting is something I could have done with shapeshifters/changing breeds/whatever. Plus, it gives the vibe of layered reality which I really like- in order to true understand an Atavism, you must look at the Beast from a number of angles all at once, a mixture of dream and reality which turned into truth. In the earlier draft, it also made the Beasts feel like madmen who believe so much that they are monsters, until they turned into them.<br /> <br /> In sort, I think that Beast is a subtle game- one about fears, shadows, dreams and myths. Simply transforming and showing your true nature is just too &quot;real&quot; for them. They are like children who play at &quot;make believe&quot;- only that their imaginations become real, and dangerous. When you look at a Beast, you know you are in danger- you can feel it in every nerve in your body- but you can't say why. They look normal, they talk normal, they don't do anything funny.. and still they can choke you to death without even looking at you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T02:05:10-07:00","id":603685,"title":"","content":"<b>LostLight</b>, I can support this view on general note - most of the time Beasts <i><b>really</b></i> should be only guys with inner soul of the Horror - but still are the moment when you should be shedding you human skin. Not often, always with a risk, but should be possible. So I made topic about hack to the game that let you do it. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/603548-beast-horror-form-hack\">You can read and comment it here</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T12:28:43-07:00","id":604006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=603646#post603646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you know, what that hooked me into Beast was the fact that they <i>don't</i> change their shape and turn into great dragons and terrible giants out of the blue. Remember the Atavism preview in the Open Blog post? that's what got me- the idea that most people look on beast on the outside and see them do weird things- but they can't see who they are. From the outside, they are just people with strange power. Those who are family, however, can see the shadows and echos of the true Beast's Soul/Horror, and the closer they are the more they see.<br /> <br /> I can't really say why I find it so appealing- but the idea of people who look half crazy and are covered by the thought of who they think they are just feels awesome from the way I see it. It both reinforce the &quot;family&quot; theme and the horror of the game, where simple shapeshifting is something I could have done with shapeshifters/changing breeds/whatever. Plus, it gives the vibe of layered reality which I really like- in order to true understand an Atavism, you must look at the Beast from a number of angles all at once, a mixture of dream and reality which turned into truth. In the earlier draft, it also made the Beasts feel like madmen who believe so much that they are monsters, until they turned into them.<br /> <br /> In sort, I think that Beast is a subtle game- one about fears, shadows, dreams and myths. Simply transforming and showing your true nature is just too &quot;real&quot; for them. They are like children who play at &quot;make believe&quot;- only that their imaginations become real, and dangerous. When you look at a Beast, you know you are in danger- you can feel it in every nerve in your body- but you can't say why. They look normal, they talk normal, they don't do anything funny.. and still they can choke you to death without even looking at you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I absolutely Love your interpretation.... It hits exactly why I fell in Love with Beast in the first place, because its the me my madness wishes it could be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/24296274/BeastThePrimordial.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":6566,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","user":"Draca","date":". 07-26-2015, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","name":"Draca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6566_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T12:38:41-07:00","id":604025,"title":"","content":"I'd have to agree, but less because it's thematic for Beasts and more because I believe that all supernaturals should have some form of &quot;Masquerade&quot; in place, whether magically enforced or not. If there are people turning into dragons in Times Square, then how is the supernatural secret at all in the World of Darkness? I was actually somewhat relieved when I learned they can't turn into those sorts of monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T13:15:33-07:00","id":604046,"title":"","content":"What is it that keeps Werewolves from transforming in the middle of Times Square? Is it different from the thing that keeps Vampires from doing it? Or Demons? Or Changelings, or Sin Eaters, or Mummies, or Mages, or even Lucifuge hunters? Pretty sure even Prometheans have some transformative/body-reshaping powers.That's all the PC groups I can think of off the top of my head. Then there are the antagonist splats, never human to begin with. What is it that keeps the Hosts in line? It's certainly not their inability to turn into freakish in-the-flesh monsters.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that secrecy as a concept should be jettisonned so that we can all be dragons flying around Times Square. I'm saying that transformative powers are something that pretty much every other gameline possesses. It's not a special concept. Everybody does it. BUT, they all do it in different ways, for different reasons, and for varying costs.<br /> <br /> IF Beasts had the ability to transform, it should be potent, and carry with it dire consequences that would make both PC and player think hard before doing it. It should also be unique and flavorful to the themes of Beast. Which is to say, it only needs to step on toes if it's designed that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T07:16:44-07:00","id":604685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JTroy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=604046#post604046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is it that keeps Werewolves from transforming in the middle of Times Square? Is it different from the thing that keeps Vampires from doing it? Or Demons? Or Changelings, or Sin Eaters, or Mummies, or Mages, or even Lucifuge hunters?</div> </div> </div> </div> Werewolves have Lunacy, which is different from what vamps, demons, lings, eaters, arisen, awakened, or hunters. Vampire, as a highly socio-political game, so their check is political. Mages need to be hidden because they suffer the paradox punishments. Changelings and Demons attract unwanted attention from the Gentry and God Machine respectively. Arisen inflict Sybaris, kind of a mix of Disbelief and Lunacy. Hunters fear reprisal from supernaturals and condemnation from mundane life. Prometheans inflict greater Disquiet with obvious power usage. Sin-Eaters have both ghosts and inner-geist that give them crap is they're obvious about anything; peace and quiet is at a minimum here.<br /> <br /> Everyone's got some way.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What is it that keeps the Hosts in line? It's certainly not their inability to turn into freakish in-the-flesh monsters. </div> </div> </div> The fear of Uratha getting wind of them as they frantically either chew through the Gauntlet, or try to gum it up for one. The ability to set trap for unwary prey for another - obvious monsters are avoided, and get little food.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-27-2015, 10:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T11:41:57-07:00","id":604885,"title":"","content":"Awesome! I had almost posed that as a rhetorical question, but this is super helpful. So, everybody's got body-morph powers, and everybody either has some sort of mystic ass cover, or a very good reason not to be revealed, or more likely, both. No reason to think a Beast wouldn't also have those same what-have-you reasons, including Heroes and just plain unwanted attention. Additionally, they'd have the concerns of whatever other gameline's social group that they attach themselves to. No reason or need for Dragons in Times Square(!!!) here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T11:56:29-07:00","id":604889,"title":"","content":"Usually both, though the &quot;ass cover&quot; is generally tied to innate abilities more than purchased stuff. For instance, vampires have the mind blurring Kiss and Lost Visage, which allows them to feed from people without someone noticing, but they've also got the Traditions to uphold, and VII/rogue ghouls/hunters to worry about. I only covered a bit of each, there's usually several built in reasons each game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T13:45:55-07:00","id":604939,"title":"","content":"Yeah, vampires are, as a rule, pretty inately subtle. But then, you've got the ones that aren't, such as certain wrecked looking Nosferatu, or Gangrel using any level of Protean beyond the 1st, especially that ultra-cool 4th level that lets you straight up take the form of your Beast. Those guys have to cover their asses through buying Obfuscate, living away from prying eyes, or suffer the consequences of being Dragons in Times Square themselves. Werewolves have Lunacy, which is very effective but even that will only carry you so far. They too can become DiTS. Mummies bust out of their tombs and hurl meteors from the sky.<br /> <br /> Basically, everyone has a little bit of passive cover, but a minority of characters will need more simply to exist. And that's fine. Personally, I think that the Beast who exists almost exclusively in Dreamland is cool. But I also don't want to be jealous of my &quot;little brother&quot;'s ability to turn into the monster that I want to be able to match pace with. And I feel like there exists within the design space a happy place where this can work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T13:52:10-07:00","id":604944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JTroy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=604939#post604939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, everyone has a little bit of passive cover, but a minority of characters will need more simply to exist. And that's fine. Personally, I think that the Beast who exists almost exclusively in Dreamland is cool. But I also don't want to be jealous of my &quot;little brother&quot;'s ability to turn into the monster that I want to be able to match pace with. And I feel like there exists within the design space a happy place where this can work.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a fairly straightforward method already available here, admittedly, and I am amused to note that it sounds like a story hook:<br /> <br /> <b>Be the most terrifying badass in New York.</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T14:01:44-07:00","id":604950,"title":"","content":"Getting back real quick to the start of the thread, in order to &quot;fix&quot; Beast, I think the most important thing <i>for me...</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JTroy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=604939#post604939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[...]But I also don't want to be jealous of my &quot;little brother&quot;'s ability to turn into the monster[...]</div> </div> </div> </div>...would be to remove the whole concept of &quot;little brother&quot; from the game and add some importance (and drawback) to placing &quot;Family Ties&quot; on people. Right now it seems....hollow as a mechanic. It's trivially easy, serves very few purpose, demands no consent from your new family member and offers drawbacks to those on which you place it while giving you bonuses only. I have no idea why a Beast <i>wouldn't </i>be running around throwing Family Ties to every super in town.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T14:11:54-07:00","id":604961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=604950#post604950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[Family Ties] demands no consent from your new family member and offers drawbacks to those on which you place it while giving you bonuses only.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are literally completely wrong on this count. Read the sidebar and the Condition's effects and look at the Satiety Potential chart again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T14:26:16-07:00","id":604973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">With regard to other player-controlled characters, the target may choose to accept the Family Ties Condition, or she may decide the Beast must use Social maneuvering </span> </div> </div> </div>so this rule only applies to other <b>player-controlled</b> characters, and even then the Beast can overrun this decision by using the same rules as they do with everyone else. NPC don't have a say in Family Ties.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">Even if the target is willing, the two still must spend considerable time together, endure common hardship, hunt together, or otherwise become close before this Condition can be applied.</span> </div> </div> </div>I'll admit this one skimmed my first reading.<br /> <br /> As for the Family Ties Condition...it <i>does </i>grant the bonuses to both the Beast and the Character, but the only drawback (Beats for <i>not playing your own game</i>) only applies to the family member, not the Beast itself. This particular effect makes sure the game is all about the Beast rather than about <b>cross-over play</b>.<br /> <br /> As for Satiety Potential, it states that you can't feed from your family members <i>as effectively</i> as from non-members...but you're already feeding from mortals so I don't understand where's the drawback, since this is not Vampire where at some point mortals are not good enough.<br /> <br /> I also understand that a Beast can only get Kinship Nightmares thanks to family members...<i>so why wouldn't a Beast run around and Family everyone?</i><br /> <br /> Passing Resemblance also asks for a Family Member, again saying that a Beast is better off getting as many friends as possible rather than a few close ones.<br /> <br /> To stay on track: I would have tried and make Beast a cross-over friendly game in the sense that it tries to get into everyone's business rather than getting everyone to care about the Beast's business.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T14:35:03-07:00","id":604997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JTroy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=604939#post604939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I also don't want to be jealous of my &quot;little brother&quot;'s ability to turn into the monster that I want to be able to match pace with. And I feel like there exists within the design space a happy place where this can work.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't see how you'd be jealous. I mean, only mortals can't see your Horror overlapping you and other supers can, don't they? And, if you really need them to see you in all your blazing glory, you can open a Primeval Pathway. Your Horror merges with you then, anywhere from Resolve dots in rounds to a full scene.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I think it'd be pretty awesome to have a scaling &quot;Merge the Dream&quot; merit, like we have Favored Form in Werewolf, advanced Demon Form stuff in DtD, and Ride the Wave in Vamp. You'd get more dice / lower Exceptional Success threshold, more time with the Primordial Pathway open, maybe higher traits in merged form, etc. Perfect way to have a visible merged form people are talking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T14:54:47-07:00","id":605050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=604973#post604973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To stay on track: I would have tried and make Beast a cross-over friendly game in the sense that it tries to get into everyone's business rather than getting everyone to care about the Beast's business.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ummm... just out of curiosity... how does Beast try to get into everyone into their business? And how would you make it more about their business beyond what Family Dinner encourages?<br /> <br /> Unless you mean fighting heroes, which I don't see as a Beast problem, since heroes are basically hunters, and that's a problem for everyone.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T15:14:38-07:00","id":605065,"title":"","content":"I'd be jealous only as a player.<br /> <br /> I love Protean, it's crazy cool how your 4th level Protean is literally an expression of the Beast* in all of it's horror.<br /> <br /> Werewolves, all about shedding their human disguise** and running with the Pack, their true family.<br /> <br /> I am not too up on Demon, but &quot;Going Loud&quot; seems to be just as thematically groovy/unique as any of the others.<br /> <br /> Basically, I think that 2E has handled the various transformation powers extremely well. I'm really excited about what Changeling and Mage will bring to the table, in terms of same. And I think the reason I'm stuck on this is because my first impression of the game was one of like... inverted Body Horror. And that really excited me because Body Horror is my favorite. And then it became apparent that I was wrong, and that's cool, but still. I can't help but wanting to shed my skin to match the colors on the inside, and glory in my visceral hideousness.<br /> <br /> *Vampire's Beast. Not <i>Beast</i> Beast.<br /> **I know, they're not literally <i>all about</i> shapeshifting. But it's pretty central, enough that human packmates are segregated from the Hunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","user":"JTroy","date":". 07-27-2015, 06:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T15:19:50-07:00","id":605070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JTroy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=605065#post605065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not too up on Demon, but &quot;Going Loud&quot; seems to be just as thematically groovy/unique as any of the others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going Loud is assuming demonic form by completely burning your Cover for extra juice. It's an emergency measure above the requisite pay grade for just manifesting your demonic form's powers normally or partially.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T15:22:33-07:00","id":605072,"title":"","content":"Beast is a game about cross-over play - and it succeeds in making sure every splat can get into the action. My point is that the game <i>seems </i>to have been designed with the idea that the PCs would always be Beasts. Again, if this was the idea, it succeeds. But since the Kinship Nightmares look like an easy way to get into other character's niche, since Beast's family mechanic is built with the Beast as the central character, since the Beast can cross dimensions without problem, etc... the game looks built to make sure the Beast always have an option and a say in the action - which again is fine if you consider the PCs are all Beasts.<br /> <br /> Let's take a coterie of vampires with a Beast in it. The whole Coterie is the Beast's family. As such, every player has a condition which states that the main character is the Beast (Bonuses if you share the spotlight with the Beast, Beats if you stop playing Vampire in order to feed the Beast)<br /> <br /> I honestly don't know how to solve this issue with the current game. It seems built around this concept and it would be hard to dislodge from there, but I believe that changing the way Family Ties work would fix a lot of it for me. Give <i>The Beast </i>incentive to care about his family rather than the other way around. If the theme is to choose your own family, make it so that choice is hard and interesting and asks a lot of questions, rather than having a condition you apply to someone to make him ruin his supernatural life in order to be with you. It looks more like a Vinculum effect than a Family Tie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T11:54:46-07:00","id":605806,"title":"","content":"Family Ties benefits go both ways. The bonuses encourage the Begotten and supernatural they've bonded with to share the limelight as a team. It doesn't really steal protagonism. The connection and other things the Beast can do for them give mechanical incentive for the recipient to care, but the Begotten has equally strong reasons to, with their own mechanical incentive.<br /> <br /> You're also putting too much of a load on the Condition alone to exemplify the themes of Beast. A lot of what you're asking for is directly correlated to the characters and the roleplaying over the mechanics; if you're asking for mechanics to be a stick rather than a carrot in exploring these themes, you're doing it wrong, or need to read the book more attentively. Treat the narrative /supported/ by the mechanics with care.<br /> <br /> Just my two cents. Mind, I'm someone who thought Beast didn't need to be fixed to begin with, but who liked a majority of the revisions anyways and /absolutely does not believe it needs any further revising that would drive it away from the original text/. <br /> <br /> Only felt like I had to comment there, so I'll go ahead and vacate the thread now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 07-28-2015, 03:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T13:39:34-07:00","id":605898,"title":"","content":"I'd rather have the mechanics be a carrot that goes both ways rather than a carrot for the Beast only. The fact that Beasts don't gain anything from getting into trouble in regards to their family is the thing bothering me - Why is the Vampire encouraged to stop doing his things to help the Beast while the Beast isn't? Why are the targets of Family Ties seen more like prey than like friends? These are the questions I'd like answered.<br /> <br /> I certainly wouldn't want the carrot to turn into a stick, that would be <i>forcing</i> families to happen rather than encouraging them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T14:02:57-07:00","id":605921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=605898#post605898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd rather have the mechanics be a carrot that goes both ways rather than a carrot for the Beast only.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've also complained about Mother's Kiss being some kind of passive-aggressive you-couldn't-do-better-without-me mechanic, so I'm really not sure what you actually <i>want</i> for the mechanics that isn't already represented by having a cordial relationship with a being who brings a pocket dimension and monstrous charisma to the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T14:17:13-07:00","id":605928,"title":"","content":"I've also calmed my opinion of said power over the course of said discussion, Satchel. These discussions are in fact in order to try and find solutions or ease misunderstandings.<br /> <br /> If I read the subtext correctly, you're saying that the &quot;mechanical&quot; advantage of being friend with a Beast is....the RP advantage of being friend with a Beast? How is that different than being friend with a Demon?<br /> <br /> As already stated, I'd have simply placed the Family Ties condition on both members of the equation rather than only on your target. And I'd have added a &quot;must be willing&quot; clause. If the theme of the game is that you <i>do </i>get to choose your family, by all means you <i>should </i>be able to choose your family.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T14:30:13-07:00","id":605943,"title":"","content":"Looking at all the times &quot;Family Ties&quot; comes up in the pdf, here's what I found.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast Benefits:</b><br /> Can create Kinship Nightmares<br /> Can use Passing Resemblance<br /> Better Family Dinners<br /> Easier to add Chambers created by the target<br /> +1 to assist or be assisted by the target<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> Worse at feeding on the target and their type of supernatural<br /> <br /> <b>Target Benefits:</b><br /> Can use the Beast's Resistance Attributes when in their presence<br /> Mother's Kiss is more effective<br /> Get 1 Beat/session if they get in trouble for associating with the Beast<br /> +1 to assist or be assisted by the Beast<br /> <br /> I don't understand how any of this &quot;makes the target feel like prey.&quot; Note that the target doesn't get Beats for &quot;playing Beast&quot; they get Beats when their relationship causes complications, which (to me, at least) is emphatically not the same thing. Also, pretty much all of the target's benefits equate to &quot;the Beast is better at supporting me,&quot; so it <i>really</i> isn't a spotlight stealer.<br /> <br /> As for why the Beast should get involved in trouble for the target's sake? To maintain Family Ties! The target can resolve the Condition at any time by &quot;cutting ties with the Beast&quot; (and get a beat for it)! From a kind of sociopathic angle, if the target dies, the Beast also loses the benefit.<br /> <br /> Idk, man. I certainly don't see a problem with doing kind of a two-way Condition so that the Beast can get Beats, too, but it seems like overkill to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T14:39:25-07:00","id":605949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=605928#post605928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I read the subtext correctly, you're saying that the &quot;mechanical&quot; advantage of being friend with a Beast is....the RP advantage of being friend with a Beast? How is that different than being friend with a Demon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Demons can't open negotiations with a supernatural third party from a position of appeal and their arena of strength is in the mortal sphere; knowing what strings to pull to get City Hall on your side isn't going to help when the Fae come calling or the Strix decide you need reminded what vampires really are, and for the most part integrating your Cover with supernatural beings is a tertiary concern liable to attract attention. Beasts have a touch of the silver-tongued devil in their ludonarrative toolbox that the fallen angels have to work at through less specialized channels.<br /> <br /> The nearest things the Unchained have to pocket dimensions in common use are specifically there as hidey-holes that you don't want people to find \u2014 the sole concession to mobility they possess just lets you open your toolshed from anywhere and get out in the same place when the coast is clear. Beasts are world-walkers with a heightened capacity for infamy and a personal hub-world that they can rearrange and authorize to suit their security needs. The degree of comparability is kind of low on that front.<br /> <br /> The space Beasts occupy in crossover is generally to be the guy who makes it really tempting to give up on the whole &quot;blending into human society&quot; thing by being better able to offer you assistance if you indulge your own supernatural nature more often and stick close to the places where they're more powerful (which may include places where you have personally lost some degree of humanity, depending on the particulars). That in turn brings that aspect of the struggle with monstrosity more to the fore if you opt to focus on it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the theme of the game is that you <i>do </i>get to choose your family, by all means you <i>should </i>be able to choose your family. </div> </div> </div>There are three themes listed at the front of the book. &quot;You choose your family&quot; is in fact the exact opposite of one of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T14:55:26-07:00","id":605966,"title":"","content":"It has always been &quot;You don't choose your family.&quot; I don't know how people miss this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T14:59:06-07:00","id":605967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=605898#post605898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd rather have the mechanics be a carrot that goes both ways rather than a carrot for the Beast only.</div> </div> </div> </div>The carrot already goes both ways. It always has.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T15:00:39-07:00","id":605968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=605072#post605072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly don't know how to solve this issue with the current game. It seems built around this concept and it would be hard to dislodge from there, but I believe that changing the way Family Ties work would fix a lot of it for me. Give <i>The Beast </i>incentive to care about his family rather than the other way around. If the theme is to choose your own family, make it so that choice is hard and interesting and asks a lot of questions, rather than having a condition you apply to someone to make him ruin his supernatural life in order to be with you. It looks more like a Vinculum effect than a Family Tie.</div> </div> </div> </div> I suggest taking a longer look at Family Dinner. While its kinda blase for getting into vampire politics, its huge for wolves and mages. You get +3 Satiety when accompanying a werewolf while they hunt down an intruder, or go off on a Sacred Hunt. Same with mages and their Mysteries. They scent something new and supernatural, they immediately go off to study it; that's their supernatural hunger. Start from there, maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T07:10:40-07:00","id":606531,"title":"","content":"As a way to build bridges rather than burn them, I'll accept the idea that the family members of the Beast have control on the relation, thus enforcing some kind of care from the Beast's part. And I'll house rule things on the go if I ever play a game with more than one player.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It has always been &quot;You don't choose your family.&quot; I don't know how people miss this. </div> </div> </div>Mostly because the first draft didn't have the themes at the front. And the Beast's ability to actually choose its family - this one kinda goes against that theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T08:24:15-07:00","id":606641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=606531#post606531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mostly because the first draft didn't have the themes at the front.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you gave up reading after the first draft you've kind of forfeit any reasonable claim on a coherent vision of how to &quot;fix&quot; the book, particularly a full month after new content finished being uploaded. The initial revisions alone are staggering in how much they add and move around.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the Beast's ability to actually choose its family - this one kinda goes against that theme. </div> </div> </div>Had Kinship powers included universal knowledge of all types of monster and the in-universe ability to fiat the appearance of other supernaturals, you would have a point, but as it stands this is pretty clearly a concession to player agency that doesn't map to character agency.<br /> <br /> A Beast that finds themself interacting with Prometheans on friendly terms is likely to pick up Family Ties with those Prometheans, but the feeling of family is, like the Homecoming, a post-hoc clarification on the sense of familiarity that got them there in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T08:30:06-07:00","id":606644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=606641#post606641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you gave up reading after the first draft you've kind of forfeit any reasonable claim on a coherent vision of how to &quot;fix&quot; the book, particularly a full month after new content finished being uploaded. The initial revisions alone are staggering in how much they add and move around.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't. I simply answer ArcaneArts question of &quot;how can people even miss this&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=606641#post606641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Had Kinship powers included universal knowledge of all types of monster and the in-universe ability to fiat the appearance of other supernaturals, you would have a point, but as it stands this is pretty clearly a concession to player agency that doesn't map to character agency.<br /> <br /> A Beast that finds themself interacting with Prometheans on friendly terms is likely to pick up Family Ties with those Prometheans, but the feeling of family is, like the Homecoming, a post-hoc clarification on the sense of familiarity that got them there in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>So your vision of the Family Ties is that it is not actual ties, but simply a strong bonding between two cousins? That the tie was always there (like the Homecoming/devouring) but that you simply clarify it? I can see this as far more in theme with the concept. I'd have liked it clarified a bit in the writing though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T20:36:46-07:00","id":643718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it#post596106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Beast controversy has been ongoing on these forums - and the RPG.net forums, from what little I know - for a while. The initial draft release attracted lots of debate, the official rewrite attracted even more.<br /> <br /> But I was wondering: for those of you who had problems with Beast, either before or after the revamp, how would you have fixed them?<br /> <br /> Myself? Well, I haven't been able to memorise the thread here, nevermind the RPG.net equivalent, but still...<br /> <br /> #1: Horrors wrapped in human flesh<br /> One of the things I liked about draft!Beast was the presentation of Beasts as literally born monsters. This is something touched on only be three other splats in the NWoD; Werewolves, Prometheans and Demons. Of those three, werewolves are often conflicted about whether or not they are happier now, demons have to feign humanity as best they can to survive, and the whole point of prometheans is to become human. Beasts, as they were presented, were something unique: monsters from birth who were actually happier when they accepted the truth.<br /> <br /> &quot;I am a monster who dreamed he was a man. But the dream is over. And the monster is awake.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's not something integral to the other lines. It was in Beast, and that was a perspective I liked for its uniqueness. I don't mind using the term &quot;Horror&quot; to refer to a Beast's inner self, because that actually a good emphasis of the theme; humans have souls, but Beasts are horrors wearing a human suit. However, the term &quot;Homecoming&quot; is essential to me; it emphasizes that a Beast is closer to a Mage or a Werewolf than to a Vampire or a Changeling. No exterior agency acted on them to make them into a Beast; it was just who they always were, and they finally accepted it.<br /> <br /> <br /> #2: Eat to live, don't live to eat<br /> Beasts need to feed. That's just how it is. Everything needs sustenance. Beasts just happen to feed on fear and horror. Something all Beasts must learn to live with is that, no matter what humans think, they are still nothing more than meat, singing to itself in the darkness. But that doesn't mean a Beast shouldn't exercise restraint. A Beast must learn how to balance its hunger with the world around them; do they try to be humane and feed &quot;reasonably&quot;, or do they embrace their dark side and gorge themselves, heedless of the destruction they cause?<br /> <br /> It's alright for Beasts to want to put a higher meaning on why they feed or how they feed, but as more than one complainer has noted, the revision's &quot;Beasts terrify humanity to teach lessons&quot; comes off as foolish and pretentious. At best, it's worth a social Z-axis foundation, but I don't think it's strong enough to be the underlying purpose of the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> #3: Heroes only in their own mind<br /> The biggest problem with draft!Beast was the very use of the term &quot;Heroes&quot; in my opinion. No matter the higher cause behind it, the basic fact is that people associate &quot;hero&quot; with &quot;good guy&quot; - it's our cultural indoctrination. And if the other side are the Heroes, then, by simple logic, we Beasts <b>must</b> be the Villains. This simple fact, more than anything, incited readers to sympathize with the Heroes and look more harshly upon the Beasts.<br /> <br /> Personally, I would call such people &quot;Slayers&quot;. It's a much less loaded term that emphasizes who and what they are: they are Killers of Beasts. Morality has nothing to do with it, except maybe as the excuse they use when called upon it. They just want to kill Beasts. That's all that matters to them.<br /> <br /> <br /> #4: Slayers are born, not made<br /> The other big problem with Heroes, from my perspective, is that they were given a mechanical creation basis. This fueled the sympathetic interpretation of them and caused the schism between Hero supporters and Beast supporters.<br /> <br /> I say that if a mortal rises up against a Beast because of that Beast's depredations, that's a Hunter, more tahn anything else. It's the universal thread that underlies all supernatural splats in the NWoD: Actions Have Consequences. Bully mortals too much, and humans will fight back. It's simple Cause and Effect.<br /> <br /> I think Slayers should just arise. There's no need for malignancy on a Beast's part. A Slayer-to-be sees a Beast, and she <b>knows</b> that they are a monster. The Beast does nothing to them; she could just be passing by in the street, buying a coffee and a donut at a local stall, sitting on the bus, and it still doesn't matter. When a Slayer sees a Beast, they undergo their own twisted version of the Homecoming, finally realizing their place in life.<br /> <br /> In fact, ideally, I think a Slayer potential should be immune to the Feasting of a hungry Horror. This would emphasize how shallow and selfish their goals are. They don't suffer from the Beast's presence, they don't experience anything to push them into accepting their role, they just open their arms and embrace it, as willingly as a Beast does.<br /> <br /> <br /> These are the things I think of when I consider what I would have done to make Beast the best I think it could be. How would you have fixed whatever problems you see or saw in Beast?</div> </div> </div> </div>#1: Born monsters and humans transformed by another monsters are classics but lack originality. I'd have gone for a &quot;Looked into the Abyss, the Abyss looked back&quot; thing. Beast would be people who kept searching into dark places (literally and/or figuratively) for Things Man Was Not Meant To Know, until their Hunger for those dark things warped or consumed their Souls, transforming them into Beasts.<br /> <br /> #2: In keeping with #1, I would have directed the Beasts Hungers toward darkness: tainted things, dark emotions, cursed items, debased creatures, corrupt people, shameful secrets. They'd be compelled to seek them out to feed on them. They'd expose the corruption, reveal the secrets, force people to face their ugly desires, steal the cursed jewels, attract and protect monstrous beings.<br /> <br /> #3: I'd see Heroes as champions of the established order; intent on keeping the Beasts from dragging the darkness to the surface and upseting the status quo. They'd be charming, inspiring, shining beacons of hope, hiding the horrible truths, making people dependant on their strength and blind to the bleak reality, and making them think they're safe, where Hungry Beasts would instead cause waves, drawing the fear and ugliness to the surface, causing fear and unrest. Heroes would hunt, fight and kill Beasts, try to erase all traces of their existences and their work, to keep the Darkness at bay like some sweep dirt under the rug, hoping that if it can't be seen it will not matter.<br /> <br /> #4: I'd have Heroes emerge as a consequences of a Beast's successes. The more people would see the darkness revealed, the more their minds would rebel against it, causing the rise of a Hero to push back the Dark and making people feel safe once again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T14:39:05-07:00","id":673439,"title":"","content":"I've only read the original kickstarter preview so this might not be applicable anymore.<br /> <br /> The biggest flaw I saw was Beast doesn't seem understand it's own themes.<br /> <br /> First of all, it's pretty apparent that Beast liberally draws inspiration from books like John Gardner's Grendel, using the theme: 'The Hero is only as great as the villain he conquers'. It attempts to flip the Monolith on its head to portray the Hero as a blind, moralizing crusader ala Disney's hunchback of notre dame.<br /> <br /> But, in Beast, the villains (i.e. the Heroes) aren't great, they're weak, pathetic, fedora tipping m'lady men (as one tawdry example). You can practically see the spittle being flung across the pages with a high authorial voice during their descriptions. Heroes aren't even near the same power levels as Beasts and are about as sympathetic and complex as a mustache twirling cartoon.<br /> <br /> <b>How to fix it? </b><br /> <br /> Beasts desperately needs some antagonist to fight against, something powerful, something great, something that its defeat *means something*. What can that be?<br /> <br /> - It can't be the Hero, they're an unfortunate person that's been pulled into this mess through no fault of their own, their creation is a by-product of the Beast feeding with low Satiety.<br /> - It can't be the Beast themselves, as there's not really a mechanic like the Shadow, or vampire's 'beast system'.<br /> <br /> Instead, I would change the main antagonist to be the Monomyth itself, deemed The Story. The only end-goal, \u2018win-state\u2019 that makes sense for Beast is destroying The Story and ending the endless cycle of Beast/Hero creation (for their Beast\u2019s soul, of course, not all Beasts).<br /> <br /> A big part of the Beasts character arc, then, would be convincing the Hero to work with the Beast, as both are necessary to destroy the Monomyth. They are both sides in this unfortunate conflict, forever linked in an eternal combat against each other, doomed to reincarnate again, and again. It would organically build a different theme, a humanist theme, one of understanding your enemies and questioning why you fight against them; scrutinizing who's the real villain in the conflict.<br /> <br /> In my version of the game, the main conflict and antagonist to overcome is *The Players and The Storyteller* themselves - the very ones describing and playing the game. The Beast confronts them why they need to tell stories and create characters that inflict untold amounts of damage and suffering in a world, only for their own amusement.<br /> <br /> But given all that, I'm going to give it another read when they release the finished version. I'm pretty confident they'll take the player feedback seriously and create a much better game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3854,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3854-darthcoffee","user":"darthcoffee","date":".  formatting, again 09-21-2015, 05:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3854-darthcoffee","name":"darthcoffee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T15:07:59-07:00","id":673457,"title":"","content":"Maybe instead of commenting while you know you're ignorant, you should go read the new documents and then given an educated insight?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T15:22:46-07:00","id":673463,"title":"","content":"Maybe you can be a little less rude. <br /> <br /> Unless they've:<br /> - Made heroes more sympathetic and drastically increased their powers<br /> - Given Beasts something to do rather than 'fight against those I create by feeding'.<br /> Then my comments still apply","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3854-darthcoffee","name":"darthcoffee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T15:24:59-07:00","id":673467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>darthcoffee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=673463#post673463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe you can be a little less rude.<br /> <br /> Unless they've:<br /> - Made heroes more sympathetic and drastically increased their powers<br /> - Given Beasts something to do rather than 'fight against those I create by feeding'.<br /> Then my comments still apply</div> </div> </div> </div>They have done both and the nearest thing to rude Arc's done is use the word &quot;ignorant&quot; to describe your self-admitted lack of knowledge about the contents of the initial revisions that have been out since the end of June.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T15:41:18-07:00","id":673483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>darthcoffee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=673463#post673463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe you can be a little less rude.<br /> <br /> Unless they've:<br /> - Made heroes more sympathetic and drastically increased their powers<br /> - Given Beasts something to do rather than 'fight against those I create by feeding'.<br /> Then my comments still apply</div> </div> </div> </div>I get banned when I'm rude. What that was was blunt.<br /> <br /> You said you didn't know the current state of affairs. That's fine, it happens, but trying to suggest changes for the game when you don't even know if your comments apply or not is, well, ruder than anything I did. It's like trying to tell people all the ways to fix Halo's story when one hasn't even played two hours of it. It's like declaring a box has a kitten in it when you last looked in it.....Well, three months ago.<br /> <br /> And yes, they've done those things. Or at least, I think so. You, you'll just have to find out if I'm right or not.<br /> <br /> See, that was a little rude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T03:18:42-07:00","id":674011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>darthcoffee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=673439#post673439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The biggest flaw I saw was Beast doesn't seem understand it's own themes.</div> </div> </div> </div> Putting aside that heroes are more sympathetic in the revised and there's lots of suggestions for using Dark Heroes from Mirrors*, you also seem to be oddly reversing the inverse. You're trying to suggest we turn Beast into the heroes of its own story. The idea is to undermine the monomyth and the violence inherent in it, not support the monomyth by recasting the roles so that the Begotten is now the hero and &quot;The Story&quot; is now the monster.<br /> <br /> I'm going to say that is exactly what the game doesn't need. Not to mention that edging far too close to CtL's Gentry territory; I would prefer to avoid that overlap. We've been telling that story for years now, and I'm interested in a new one.<br /> <br /> I would also like to say that I suspect you've missed the actual central theme. While feeding your Hunger and warding off heroes is part of the story, its actually only a part of it - Vampire is far more than drinking blood and protecting your territory, and Mage has more to it than scrutinizing magic to buy up Arcana dots. The central driving story force in Beast is actually crossover. The game isn't just highly crossover compatable, its also a central drive of the game.<br /> <br /> Beast, in many ways, is an inverted HtV game. Hunter focuses on PC splats to track down and capture/kill - there's a reason the majority of their books focus on hunting vamps, wolves, mages, prommies, fae, sin-eaters, mummies, and demons, with a side of fellow hunters (sometimes turned Slasher). Unlike most other games, crossover isn't really a potential plot hook or style here. For Hunter and Beast, its a central one. The difference is that, in Beast, you're not on the hunt to kill or capture, but to make friends and build a family. And, yes, Family is another major aspect of Beast - there's a reason we call beasts the Children and the Begotten, and a reason why we call the cotorie-equivalent the brood.<br /> <br /> <br /> * As of the last revision, it feels like that heroes are still roughly on par with hunters in terms of power level, which means that, no, they're not a match for the Children in a straight up battle without anathema in full force. Which is why people are suggesting the Dark Heroes in the mirrors book, and combining the two. Having the D.H. powered by the Temnos/Bright Dream and their super-ability with skills actually does a fairly good job of keeping the themes of BtP's heroes, while making them a greater challenge in a direct battle. Combine with the other abilities, and its actually a pretty interesting spread of abilities. <br /> <br /> That said, the low power of the heroes might actually be deliberate, so as to keep the whole &quot;plucky underdog&quot; vibe of hunters around. The whole over-confident, knowing I can crush them at any time vibe might be an important vibe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 09-22-2015, 06:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T06:59:46-07:00","id":674140,"title":"","content":"@darthcoffee A few things. Being told your ignorant isn't an insult. It just means that you needed to do more homework. As everyone else mentioned heroes got quite a tune up between drafts. <br /> <br /> As MCN points out, crossover is a core theme of the game (actually more of a theme of the metagame). However (and here's where my opinion diverges from MCN) it isn't the only theme and the second draft doesn't do enough to adequately prepare player or gamemaster for explaining why reclusive societies like vampires and werewolves would accept a Beast. Notions like Family and Kin are underdeveloped and at no time does it ever explore Beast relationships with humans in anything beyond a &quot;it's food&quot; and &quot;teach it a lesson.&quot;<br /> <br /> My hope is that the final draft expands on both Family and Kinship and shows us something beyond the heavy handed deus ex machina of &quot;hey, mechanical benefits.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T07:31:30-07:00","id":674160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=674140#post674140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the second draft doesn't do enough to adequately prepare player or gamemaster for explaining why reclusive societies like vampires and werewolves would accept a Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>A small reminder here that <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/641760-beast-changeling-kinships?p=651370#post651370\">their societies are not Beast's point of interface with other gamelines' supernaturals.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T08:11:49-07:00","id":674216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=674160#post674160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A small reminder here that <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/641760-beast-changeling-kinships?p=651370#post651370\">their societies are not Beast's point of interface with other gamelines' supernaturals.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, my thoughts are that Beast's don't get in with the &quot;Big&quot; groups (Although i'd imagine the Ordo Dracul would love to study them) but on a more personal level... they get to meet the Individual not the organization. They meet singular Vampires, Werewolves and Magi and make friends... slowly because they are the Outsider, they aren't... Like the rest, yet they feel right.<br /> <br /> As many soldiers would say &quot;Family isn't just about Blood, it's about who you'd fight for and who'd fight for you&quot; Beast's are like the Cousin who you only know about because you meet them once, but you know they'd do whatever they can for you if you only ask.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T08:18:13-07:00","id":674219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=674160#post674160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A small reminder here that <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/641760-beast-changeling-kinships?p=651370#post651370\">their societies are not Beast's point of interface with other gamelines' supernaturals.</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You've tried making this point before but, you're argument fails to compel me. Problem number one for your interpretation is that the text of neither draft supports it. Nowhere does either of them say that Beasts are hooking up with the dregs for some kind of weird mutual survival.<br /> <br /> Societal concerns and social dynamic are a huge part of WoD games, especially games like Changeling, Vampire, and Werewolf. If Beasts only count a society's rejects as Kin then Kinship isn't about being supernatural (which IMO it shouldn't have been anyway). Since the existing narrative goes to great lengths to focus on how Beasts only count supernatural creatures as Kin (so no Hunters and Mages are marginal), I don't think your explanation fits with the actual intentions of Beast's development team. The fact is, just looking at the existing mechanics and dearth of exposition for <i>why</i>, Beasts (vis-a-vis other supernaturals) look more like Remoras than Sharks.<br /> <br /> As a reader I'm left unsure what it is about joining teams with the other lines' rejects that makes Beast a crossover game. Mechanically they're just Remoras coming along for the ride.<br /> <br /> It's not <i>really</i> a crossover game, is it? It wants to be but, the implementation falls flat (at least insofar as drafts 1 and 2 are concerned). All we really have is some mechanics and a lot of metagamerly gobbledy-gook.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, even the 2nd draft is a narrative that tries to do too much and fails to bring all of its disparate ideas into a cohesive whole. I hope that the final draft is as much improved over the 2nd as the 2nd draft was over the 1st.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 09-22-2015, 11:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T08:20:54-07:00","id":674222,"title":"","content":"I somewhat disagree with the notion that they're more likely to join up with solitaires and antagonists(though they certainly aren't less likely), but it's worth reiterating that Beasts don't care or worry about joining other monster's societies. Keep your Elysiums and Consiliums, the Beast doesn't want to be named the Constable of the Freehold, or hell, even consider a courtier. They connect with <i>individuals</i> as friends and family. That's usually meansthat Beasts don't become a big enough blip on any Prince's/Queen's/Old One's radar,and when it is, it's often treated as an exceptional case based on how things proceed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T08:44:47-07:00","id":674261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=674222#post674222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I somewhat disagree with the notion that they're more likely to join up with solitaires and antagonists(though they certainly aren't less likely),</div> </div> </div> </div>Clarifying here that it's not so much about probability as it is simplicity and inertia \u2014 monsters with nowhere else to go are both easier to pick up and more likely to stay on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T08:51:03-07:00","id":674267,"title":"","content":"The big question about how any society reacts to a Beast is largely dependent on what an individual Beast does to garner the attention of that society. THe broad stereotypes provided by each template about Beasts is a good measuring stick, a decent way to start brainstorming ideas, but the fundamental problem at hand is that the thing you're asking about is something that is best answered in game. A freehold is going to respond to a Beast who gained their attention by blowing up a strip mall differently from a factional krewe who met the Beast when she was being the life of the party at the last Wake. Similarly, a traditional Mesen-Nebu guildmaster, who will even sort of applaud those who steal from them, is going to respond differently to a Collector than they would to a Ravager, the former with favor and the latter with disdain(maybe). A less traditional Alchemist is more likely to be pissed at either one, but might respond favorably to the workings of a Tyrant.<br /> <br /> This is a thing that can be talked about in later supplement, but it's largely not useful to hypothesize about how society reacts when it quite frankly comes down to each person's game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-22-2015, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T08:52:46-07:00","id":674269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=674261#post674261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clarifying here that it's not so much about probability as it is simplicity and inertia \u2014 monsters with nowhere else to go are both easier to pick up and more likely to stay on.</div> </div> </div> </div>A fair point I admit to not thinking about this time around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T09:16:58-07:00","id":674311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=674261#post674261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clarifying here that it's not so much about probability as it is simplicity and inertia \u2014 monsters with nowhere else to go are both easier to pick up and more likely to stay on.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yZAY-78zhmw\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Shake my hand, come on boys, Won't you shake a Poor Sinners hand?&quot; </a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T15:24:26-07:00","id":674618,"title":"","content":"For me, personally, I find <b><i>Beast</i></b> to be too...happy.<br /> <br /> The main grievance I have is that the <i><b>Beasts </b></i>don't feel like they have anything to worry about. They realize that they are <i><b>Beasts</b></i> and that they have been forced into this role for some grand narrative, locked into some story in which they <i>must</i> be the villain. And they're pretty okay with it. Sure, there are some crazy people who want to play <i><b>Hero </b></i>and attempt to slay them, but it's all good to them.<br /> <br /> Granted, I am simplifying the concepts of <b><i>Beast</i></b> into what I feel it all relates to, but that is what I see when I think of how <b><i>Beast</i></b> currently is. Tonally, it's pretty feel-good. Two of the <b><i>Beasts</i> </b>in the story are gay and in a relationship (I have no issue with that, being a gay male myself who likes seeing little things such as that in games), but given that <b><i>Beast</i> </b>plays up the idea that there will be people who will hate you for what you are, it kinda hit the nail on the head a little too hard. <br /> <br /> For me, I feel that <i><b>Beast</b>, </i>or at least the inspiration for the tone of <b><i>Beast</i></b>, should have shifted away from <i>Beauty and the Beast</i>, where it focuses on the idea that Beast is a good person despite his outward appearance, and should have taken a bit from <i>The Tiger's Bride</i>. For those of you not familiar, <i>The Tiger's Bride</i> is a short story written by Angela Carter that is based on the classic story of <i>Beauty and the Beast</i> but reverses the idea by having the Beast be a literal tiger who hides his nature and masquerades as a human. The Beauty of the story, feeling a kinship with the Beast due to her being treated similarly to an animal due to her status as a young woman, realizes her own nature and allows the Beast to lick the skin off her body, revealing that she is also a tiger. I would have loved for <i><b>Beast </b></i>to have incorporated that idea for the actual <i><b>Beasts</b>. </i>Granted, <b><i>Beasts</i></b> start off as humans unaware of their true nature, but there doesn't feel like there is any conflict between who they are/were as humans and who they are in reality. Being seen as human by mortals isn't something that is truly awkward or conflicting for them; it's more of a convenience so they can go munching on fear when the lights go out without anyone suspecting a thing.<br /> <br /> As for the treatment of <i><b>Heroes</b></i>, I would have preferred to interpret their relationship as, rather than a mortal wielding a stick against a nightmare-ish creature who can crush them like a grape, to something more modern and even, like Batman going against his Rogues Gallery. Bruce Wayne became Batman when something unfortunate occurred, causing him to fight back in order to keep Gotham safe. This, in turn, inadvertently meant that the many individuals who he faced were, in some way, influenced by his presence. Granted, they were all a bit loony before he came to exist, but his constant existence molded the way they reacted. <b><i>(Note: I'm basically taking this from the TvTropes website, the Trope &quot;Create Your Own Villain&quot;, and the Batman section. I'm not a devout follower of Batman nor do I feel that I have a strong understanding of the Batman series, but I do know that some of Batman's reoccurring antagonists were influenced by Batman himself)</i></b> Each villain as some sort of rhyme and reason to do what they feel should be done and Batman responds by preventing them from doing what they want to do. Is Poison Ivy wrong for being an environmentalist and wanting people to take care of the world around them? No, not exactly. Is she wrong for inspiring people with fear with her man-eating plants and mind-influencing pollen? That is a more relativistic question, where Poison Ivy feels that she is in the right and Batman <i>(and, presumably, most of Gotham)</i> feels she is in the wrong. I feel the same should be reflected in <b><i>Beast</i>. </b>Is a Tyrant who wants to invert the power structure of some societal belief wrong for doing so in some vicious manner? Possibly no, but there will be someone who feels that it should not change and rise up to prevent said Tyrant from doing so. Maybe to fill some void within themselves, sure, but also because, in some way, that is what they feel is right.<br /> <br /> Of course, that is all my own opinion. <b><i>Beast</i></b>, despite whatever grievances people have with it, is a fine game where it stands now. Some people may be confused and want clarification, and that's fine. Some people may want there to be changes in order to better represent what they believe <b><i>Beast</i></b> should represent, and that's also fine. Objectively, I think <b><i>Beast </i></b>is a wonderful addition to the <i><b>World of Darkness</b></i> and allows players to be something that has not been well represented in the other game lines. Subjectively, I feel that <b><i>Beast</i></b> may not be thematically tasty for my palate. <br /> <br /> But what do I know? I may have interpreted things incorrectly and may have created my own inferences with no basis whatsoever. Feel free to comment or discuss so that I, and maybe others, will be able to understand. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T18:13:57-07:00","id":674764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=674219#post674219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've tried making this point before but, you're argument fails to compel me. Problem number one for your interpretation is that the text of neither draft supports it. Nowhere does either of them say that Beasts are hooking up with the dregs for some kind of weird mutual survival.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would indeed be a problem if it were more than remotely my point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Societal concerns and social dynamic are a huge part of WoD games, especially games like Changeling, Vampire, and Werewolf. </div> </div> </div>Whose constituents are individual members which Beasts approach from an initial position as outsiders to those societies and dynamics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If Beasts only count a society's rejects as Kin then Kinship isn't about being supernatural (which IMO it shouldn't have been anyway). </div> </div> </div>Your O aside, you're slipping a foreign &quot;only&quot; into my point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Since the existing narrative goes to great lengths to focus on how Beasts only count supernatural creatures as Kin (so no Hunters and Mages are marginal), I don't think your explanation fits with the actual intentions of Beast's development team. </div> </div> </div>The story running through the chapter fiction ends with the main character holed up in a lake with two vampires who abandoned what little contact they had with their society \u2014 &quot;But more than one vampire, in a town this size?&quot; \u2014 to live with him for reasons that are best summed up with the line, &quot;She's gotta get rid of the new fucker, or they both gotta leave town.&quot; Everyone in Ben's family winds up an outcast from mortal and vampire society.<br /> <br /> Totally unintentional.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As a reader I'm left unsure what it is about joining teams with the other lines' rejects that makes Beast a crossover game. </div> </div> </div>As a reader you displayed a bizarre obsession with using the word &quot;schoolmarm&quot; to describe attempts to use supernatural necessity as a basis for mundane warning, so I'm ill-inclined to trust your readings when it comes to thematics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T20:27:34-07:00","id":674888,"title":"","content":"@satchel I'm sorry, I must have missed it. I could swear that you were saying that the societies of other supernaturals weren't the point. Then you say you aren't saying that. What were you saying? I've lost track among all of your tangents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 09-22-2015, 11:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T20:31:30-07:00","id":674890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=674216#post674216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed, my thoughts are that Beast's don't get in with the &quot;Big&quot; groups (Although i'd imagine the Ordo Dracul would love to study them) but on a more personal level... they get to meet the Individual not the organization. They meet singular Vampires, Werewolves and Magi and make friends... slowly because they are the Outsider, they aren't... Like the rest, yet they feel right.<br /> <br /> As many soldiers would say &quot;Family isn't just about Blood, it's about who you'd fight for and who'd fight for you&quot; Beast's are like the Cousin who you only know about because you meet them once, but you know they'd do whatever they can for you if you only ask.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except neither draft delves into the whole &quot;who would you fight for&quot; in-the-trenches mentality notion of family. <br /> <br /> Honestly, this is the shallowest interpretation of family. Folks are focusing only on the &quot;I get to choose&quot; factor and not the &quot;we need you to do 10 to 20 for the family&quot; aspect. Watch Sons of Anarchy sometime and see the whole obligations portion of Family that is missing from both of these drafts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 09-22-2015, 11:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T20:49:47-07:00","id":674903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=674888#post674888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry, I must have missed it. I could swear that you were saying that the societies of other supernaturals weren't the point. Then you say you aren't saying that. What were you saying? I've lost track among all of your tangents.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm saying that Beasts do not have to be in the thick of any of the various supernatural societies for their line to facilitate crossover play, that the default assumptions of the text by no means present such involvement as the norm, and that Beasts with family among the isolated and entropic groups in a given splat tend to eat better and require negotiation of fewer of the social minefields predicated on having to destroy, deprive, or decapitate to sustain oneself.<br /> <br /> A Beast in a Promethean-based game is going to manage higher Satiety and a longer-lived family with a pack of Pandorans and the odd Centimanus than with a conventional adherent to the Pilgrimage. A Beast in a Mummy-based game has similar odds siding with the actual cannibal servants of the Devourer or the incarnate vessels of the vengeful architects of civilization over the sporadically active Law-empowered automatons. Similar examples exist throughout, particular when there's explicit framework for making Family Ties with ferals.<br /> <br /> That you think this means I believe the <i>only</i> creatures Beasts can call kin are the lone monsters of the other splats in contravention of the basic mechanics and narrative framework provided about Kinship is not a testament to my circuitousness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T10:12:20-07:00","id":675345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=674618#post674618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, personally, I find <b><i>Beast</i></b> to be too...happy.</div> </div> </div> </div> Its happy when, by nature, you're someone that voyeuristically feeds on people's loss and defeat? I guess I can't reconsile happy with effectively playing a sadist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T10:53:28-07:00","id":675398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=675345#post675345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Its happy when, by nature, you're someone that voyeuristically feeds on people's loss and defeat? I guess I can't reconsile happy with effectively playing a sadist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Further to this, you can feed reasonably harmlessly, but it's only small meals you have to eat often, and you risk your inner monster going out to feed itself (in fairness, though, that only seems to cause vivid nightmares). You want a good meal? It has to be elaborate, specific or heinous. You want a really good meal? It has to be all of those. The fuller you get, the less of a general danger you represent to people, but the worse you have to be to get there. Unlike a vampire, your feeding can't be hidden behind an enforced sense of bliss. You could restrict yourself to people who deserve, but they don't come along every day, so you have to deal with the temptation to let deserve slide into &quot;deserve.&quot; Finding a balance you can live with doesn't seem happy to me, it seems like a grind. (Unless you're playing a straight-up bad guy of course).<br /> <br /> <br /> For me, though, Beast doesn't particularly need fixing. The only thing I'd like to see is the adoption of a philosophical splat (I kind of think of Family and Hunger as two X's, despite it not being impossible for Hunger to change). In this case, the teaching deal would be one such philosophy. Another would take Family as an imperative: that is, the purpose of Beasts is to seek out other supernaturals and become middle men and social glue for them. One would follow their humanity, and live relatively ordinary lives, balanced by their new powers and concerns (something I think Beast is oddly suited to, given its outr\u00e9 protagonists). There might be one that takes feeding their Hunger as a righteous imperative (which might either replace any conscience they have or uneasily coexist with it).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T11:16:42-07:00","id":675445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=675345#post675345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Its happy when, by nature, you're someone that voyeuristically feeds on people's loss and defeat? I guess I can't reconsile happy with effectively playing a sadist.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I suppose &quot;happy&quot; is a bit too bright of a definition. For me, I see <b><i>Beast</i></b> to be happy in the way that I see <b><i>Geist</i></b> as happy. It is a balancing act to feed in a meaningful way to not go crazy or hurt other people, but it seems to be not that big of a deal. If you want, you could play monster and just be a terrible person and there really isn't anything to stop you from doing so other than storytelling limits and Heroes. As I read into it, it feels that <b><i>Beast</i></b> doesn't have a feeling of dread that most of the other game lines have (<b><i>Vampires</i></b> deal with the inevitability of death and figuring out how to live out their un-life, <b><i>Prometheans</i></b> are struggling to be human and cause everyone around them to hate them, <b><i>Changelings</i></b> worry about being found by the True Fae and being taken back, etc.), similar to how <b><i>Sin-Eaters</i></b> enjoy their second chance at life without <i>really</i> having to worry. <br /> <br /> I guess that by &quot;happy&quot;, I mean &quot;able to live comfortably without any real, tangible consequences that they have to worry about&quot;. Granted, any of the game line creatures can be jerks and just wipe out humanity, but most of them have some repercussions or actual, credible threats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T12:11:17-07:00","id":675579,"title":"","content":"Its possible to live comfortably withotu any real, tangible consequences in pretty much any game line. Set yourself up with a nice territory out of the way of other packs, and you can pull it off easily. Mages lack any drama outside of their obsession with seeking magic. Be a recluse from mage society, live mostly like a human, and viola, no drama. Changelings that kill their fetch and reuinite with their family can mostly avoid most of the Huntsman drama. Demons can move away from any Infrastructure and do the whole Mountain Man routine and not worry about angels in the backarea of nowhere. A vampire can set up a herd of terminally-ill ghouls and guilt-free feed off them down through the years, and set up in some area away from vampire society.<br /> <br /> There's certain buy-ins for every game. Prometheans want to become human, full stop. None of this &quot;better than human without Flux&quot; ideas that are floating around. Mages seek Mysteries. Changelings build new homes so they'll no longer be Lost. Demons engage the God Machine in their search for enlightenment and Hell. For Beast, its the search for Family. That family can be other supernaturals, it can be other Begotten in your Brood, it can be the heroes. Its as much of a drive for them as politics is for vampires and fighting the Fae is for the Lost. <br /> <br /> All of them have the potential to be living comfortably without problems. If the whole looking for Family thing isn't to your tastes, that's one thing. But saying we're lacking the kind of worrisome drama the other games is another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T13:35:20-07:00","id":675681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=675579#post675579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's certain buy-ins for every game. <b>...</b> For Beast, its the search for Family. That family can be other supernaturals, it can be other Begotten in your Brood, it can be the heroes. Its as much of a drive for them as politics is for vampires and fighting the Fae is for the Lost.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will say that I agree with this. <b><i>Beast</i></b> does at least have a running theme of looking for family, and I do enjoy this aspect because it speaks for the underlining theme of &quot;finding your place in the world&quot; that <b><i>Beast </i></b>has <i>(Feeling that you are, in some way, different, realizing that you aren't what you were raised to believe, and searching for like-minded people or people with similar experiences, kind of a reasonable stretch; Vampires have politics as a means of dealing with un-life and death and Changelings deal with the True Fae as a metaphor for abuse and confronting the issue, at least as far as I read into it). </i>I find the fact that at least two of the <b><i>Beasts</i></b> being gay and in a relationship with each other to be too obvious of a metaphor for what <b><i>Beast </i></b>represents, but I'm willing to allow it to pass. <br /> <br /> I suppose what I want in terms of worrisome drama relates to the <i>Slumbering</i> and <i>Starving</i> Conditions, especially in how Beats are received from the two. With <i>Slumbering</i>, a Beast may have a chance to be rejected due to the fact that they are, effectively, human for the time being. With <i>Starving</i>, a Beast may end up doing something that they didn't mean to as a side-effect of going nutsy-cuckoo and hurting someone they care about. These two ideas tie in <i>very well</i> with the theme of finding family because it deals with the idea that the <b><i>Beast</i></b> may do something that will alienate themselves from their new family. It's something minor, but it's an important idea and I feel that it should be expanded upon. A <b><i>Beast</i></b> may be rejected by someone they were close to because they were <i>too</i> monstrous, so the <b><i>Beast</i></b> feels that they must hide some harsh aspect of themselves when they find someone else. A <b><i>Beast</i></b> may end up killing a member of their family, causing them to be abandoned by the people they thought were family. I feel like these ideas weren't expanded upon aside from in the Conditions. If they were in the book, then I must have overlooked them and I would be grateful if I could be pointed in the right direction for them.<br /> <br /> I apologize if my arguments seem to be poorly-formed or cyclical, but it is a hang-up that I have with Beast that I feel has yet to be resolved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T14:28:39-07:00","id":675699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=675681#post675681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose what I want in terms of worrisome drama relates to the <i>Slumbering</i> and <i>Starving</i> Conditions, especially in how Beats are received from the two. With <i>Slumbering</i>, a Beast may have a chance to be rejected due to the fact that they are, effectively, human for the time being. With <i>Starving</i>, a Beast may end up doing something that they didn't mean to as a side-effect of going nutsy-cuckoo and hurting someone they care about. These two ideas tie in <i>very well</i> with the theme of finding family because it deals with the idea that the <b><i>Beast</i></b> may do something that will alienate themselves from their new family.</div> </div> </div> </div> True that. Its like that one story of the vamp that heard about a beast that killed one of his broodmate's human sister. The vamp was surprised and a bit confused over the issue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's something minor, but it's an important idea and I feel that it should be expanded upon. A <b><i>Beast</i></b> may be rejected by someone they were close to because they were <i>too</i> monstrous, so the <b><i>Beast</i></b> feels that they must hide some harsh aspect of themselves when they find someone else. A <b><i>Beast</i></b> may end up killing a member of their family, causing them to be abandoned by the people they thought were family. I feel like these ideas weren't expanded upon aside from in the Conditions. If they were in the book, then I must have overlooked them and I would be grateful if I could be pointed in the right direction for them. </div> </div> </div> I don't think that it was really specifically stated, but there is definitely a vibe like that through the book. Take Family Dinner, for instance. Daeva tend to form large herds they fall in love with. That kind of close knit feeding, for the vamp, is ideal. For the beast? They get nothing out of it. The Children want to push the vampire to go out and have a real <i>hunt</i>. Track down someone on the street, reel them in, and bite them. Act like a &quot;real vampire.&quot; Do you know who else encourages vampires to act like that? The strix. Look at Kinship Nightmares; the Begotten like low Wisdom mages over high.<br /> <br /> Every PC supernatural has a human side to them, and a monstrous side. The beasts are in tune with that monstrous side. They want to encourage that. They're pushing the supernaturals to engage in the worst aspects of their nature. Do you want to be friends with people like that? Its toxic. The best friend of the Children are the Scelesti, the Belial's Brood, and the Pure. Think on that for a minute. Do the Beasts really want to be like that? Do they want to push their friends to be like that? And that's at High Satiety. At Low Satiety? You're encouraged to bounce between hitting 4 Satiety, then frivalously spending Satiety to go back to Low. Then indulging your Hunger in small but careless ways, which, in all honesty, are meant to attract heroes and hunters. What supernatural wants to attract hunters?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I apologize if my arguments seem to be poorly-formed or cyclical, but it is a hang-up that I have with Beast that I feel has yet to be resolved. </div> </div> </div> No worries, this is nothing more than a friendly discussion. I'm not trying to argue with you or prove you wrong, I'm just trying to discuss an alternative view point. I mean, I'm not a writer for Beast, so we're just fans debating the work. Neither of us can say we're right or wrong until one of the devs come by.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T17:21:36-07:00","id":675832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=675699#post675699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Children want to push the vampire to go out and have a real <i>hunt</i>. Track down someone on the street, reel them in, and bite them. <b>Act like a &quot;real vampire.&quot;</b> <br /> <br /> <b>...</b><br /> <br /> Every PC supernatural has a human side to them, and a monstrous side. The beasts are in tune with that monstrous side. They want to encourage that. They're pushing the supernaturals to engage in the worst aspects of their nature. Do you want to be friends with people like that? Its toxic.</div> </div> </div> </div>That...is actually an incredible and genius interpretation of <b><i>Beasts</i></b> and I love it, especially the sentence that I bolded in your quote. It makes it seem like, despite the fact that <b><i>Beasts</i></b> feel as if they are trapped into the villain role, they are attempting to hamfist other supernaturals into roles themselves. They are trapped because they are inadvertently perpetuating the Grand Scheme Cosmic Story they are trying to break. I love it so much.<br /> <br /> Thank you for sharing that. That does add a dimension to what <b><i>Beasts</i></b> are for me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T18:22:08-07:00","id":675872,"title":"","content":"There's a relationship here between evil and natural consequences of the id.<br /> <br /> It is not a tea and biscuits kind of relationship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T18:42:40-07:00","id":675896,"title":"","content":"Glad I could be of service!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T19:55:00-07:00","id":675969,"title":"","content":"I would have hired me and paid me lots of money to write the book. Actually writing the book may or may not have occurred after receiving said money.<br /> <br /> It's probably a good thing I don't write books.<br /> <br /> Hey, at least I'm honest.<br /> <br /> And at least I probably made you chortle at &quot;lots of money&quot; and &quot;for writing an RPG book&quot; wound up in the same sentence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T00:34:24-07:00","id":677381,"title":"","content":"I'd focus on a Theme of Victimization, and a Mood of Tragic Absurdity.<br /> <br /> I would try to turn narrative into Narrative. Beasts believe that there is some outside force (perhaps even the Mother of Monsters) that drive the Horrors and Heroes to be what they are, that tries to dictate that the Horror will terrorize the populace only to be defeated by the Hero who will share his wisdom with the outside world. But the Narrative doesn't fit the real world anymore, especially not the modern one. Perhaps it never did. Teaching lessons through pain and fear without proper authority has be disapproved of for centuries, perhaps millennium. Rare is the Beast who has such authority, rarer still is the one who limits their feeding solely to the exercise of same. In stories wolves can blow in houses and eat their inhabitants as a demonstration on why work ethic is so important, but no one's going to care about work ethic if you do that in real life. The Horror doesn't care - it just wants to eat. <br /> <br /> (Maybe this is why Demons aren't kin. The Narrative teaches wisdom through pain, while the God-Machine teaches insignificance through dehumanization, or so the Beasts who know of it say.)<br /> <br /> And Heroes aren't Heroes anymore. They've gone from being Heroic to being Protagonists, from making mankind better to making mankind better because of <i>them. </i>It may seem like a small change, but that shift of focus from the people being helped to the person doing the helping was warped them, broken them somehow. The Primordial Dream stops attracting those who seek to spread wisdom and starts attracting those who need a purpose, who need to feel special in this darkcog world. Whether or not this too is a side-effect of the God-Machine, directly or indirectly, is impossible to tell for sure. Protagonists have stopped seeing people as beneficiaries and now see them as adulators, lackeys, and collateral damage.<br /> <br /> A Hero's story has an ending. A Protagonist has endless and ever-escalating sequels. When the Protagonist kicks in the door seeking the Beast's head and the Horror lets out a feral scream that is equal parts rage, confidence, and hunger the Beast can't help but feel stuck in a predetermined scenario written by someone who has long since forgotten the original point and just wants to see excitement and blood, <i>anything</i> that will pierce the lull of humanity and hopefully get them to learn <i>something.</i> Of the Beast, the Horror, and the Protagonist only the Beast has a vague awareness of how the Narrative presses on them all, of how they are used for a purpose that often doesn't work as intended. They are the only ones with the self-awareness needed to evade or break the Narrative (and they know it), and to do it they'll have to not only fight off Protagonists but find a way to guide a Horror anywhere but the meat-filled path that leads to oblivion.<br /> <br /> You want your purpose? It's a tricky position at best and an outmoded rationalization at worse. You want your power? It comes in spades, spades which will dig countless spiritual and literal graves. You want your place? It's not among the humanity you were expecting your place to be but among the darkest shadows of the world. You will have the chance to reach out to monsters and find that even they are deserving of a place to call haven and a group to call family, both of which you can help them build. You can protect them with your powers while still appearing as human to other humans, helping to guard the secrets of your brood. You can be their best friend - and the Horror inside you can be their worst enemy, gladly leading them off a moral precipice if you let it. For all the power the Horror gives you you feel its hunger even more.<br /> <br /> The Beast will be screaming at you to justify as badly as you need to (or even better, to cut through the justification crap entirely) to reduce the world to victims you feed on and enemies you have to fend off so you can keep feeding. It's not going to be a noble scream, the bellowing of a dragon demanding to display its power. It's going to be an almost pathetic screeching that you take that iPhone right now because he clearly doesn't care enough about it but you will, even when you know you'd just add it to the pile. And in the darker moments your voice will join its. <i>This is absurd,</i> you tell yourself. <i>I don't need to justify myself, and even when I do the world doesn't listen. Screw them.</i> It'll be easy, even tempting - what human doesn't fantasize about bringing reprisals upon others while escaping repercussions themselves? But that's a trap, and if you do that it's over. You and your brood'll enjoy the lack of inhibitions, sure, but only until you bite off more than you can chew and the Narrative summons the actors who will bring your part to a violent end.<br /> <br /> The Narrative victimizes the Beasts, giving them paths that all say &quot;TO THE QUICKSAND.&quot; It victimizes Horrors, birthing them with the instinct to fatten themselves in ways that call in their own butchers. It victimizes Protagonists, giving them their purpose and praises while taking away the humanity that would make it worthwhile. And these three in turn prey upon humanity, leaving them victimized and traumatized far more often than they are left wiser, giving them power that is barely significant at the best of times. Everyone is given power but no one is given the means to use it meaningfully or (for Horrors and Protagonists) even the desire to do so.<br /> <br /> No one except the Beasts who have a chance to turn away from this, to give themselves a higher purpose that will give them a chance to escape their predetermined fates. If they work together, with themselves and with their kin, perhaps they can say they teach wisdom through pain and not have it feel hollow. Perhaps they can evade or even beat the Narrative and forge a Legend all their own. This is something all Beasts realize sooner or later, something they all tell each other. And yet it is who they are that cries out in a voice so much louder. Can a Beast listen to their families and control their Horror? Do they even want to?<br /> <br /> I know the 2nd revision makes a lot of inroads towards this, but I really hope they can work towards making all the parts into a cohesive whole.<br /> <br /> And if players are willing to make themselves uncomfortable, I'd focus on the idea of victim-blaming. To teach a lesson through pain presupposes that the student is deserving of pain. Stories take this for granted, and Horrors will do the same. To a Horror everyone deserves what they get and it is on them to learn to avoid being victims again. Fault and Proportionality mean nothing to a Horror, and they'll gladly exploit ambiguities or even contradictions in human morality, which means a Beast will hear things like this all day:<br /> &quot;That guy said his race was better than yours. Teach him respect by breaking his arm in (and break the other one when he calls your kind violent thugs)&quot;<br /> &quot;They're ignoring their fellow man. Make yourself noticed. Whatever they drop, you keep.&quot;<br /> &quot;He's fat because he has no self-control. He's fat because he'd rather feed himself than those starving around him. Show him what it means to be a meatbag.&quot;<br /> &quot;That one who commits microaggressions? That one who makes everyone else miserable by being hypersensitive about microaggressions? That one trying to silence people who are talking about microaggressions? That's breakfast, lunch, and dinner right there.&quot;<br /> &quot;That pastor who speaks so proudly of his congregation? Burn his house down and teach him how charitable they really are.&quot;<br /> <br /> For every feeding the Horror will say &quot;they deserved it,&quot; whether anything was taught or not. Whether the Beast agrees, when the Beast agrees, and how far the Beast will go to decide who &quot;deserves it&quot; should say a lot about the Beast and how the world around him reacts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8064-mp122984","name":"mp122984","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T13:35:13-07:00","id":692873,"title":"","content":"I think I would have focused more on actually <i>being</i> a Beast. Players are actual immortal beasts out of legend who were slowly worn down by the passing of time and diminished into humans, often forgetting what they were for large periods of time. Prosaic reality generally binds you as a human, but Beasts have the ability to force some sort of a &quot;mythic break&quot; where the world around them temporarily changes to become simpler and more storylike -- more vibrant and mythic, but with some essential part of what makes it <i>real</i> in the modern sense suppressed or removed. While this is in effect in their area, they can recall their true selves and take on their beast form.<br /> <br /> Heroes are reincarnated figures of legend. Like Beasts, they feel this yearning for a simpler mythic world, but unlike Beasts, they don't have the power to force a mythic break on the world themselves -- they can only do it when attacking Beasts. And some of them (the ones that you're likely to end up fighting, generally) find the rush of that simple black-and-white mythic world exhilarating, so they hunt Beasts in order to go back there. Heroes often see the mythic reality as more &quot;real&quot;, as if they're tearing away illusions by hunting Beasts, but the truth is more complicated -- a Beast actually <i>is</i> also a human.<br /> <br /> I would generally tone down on the moralizing aspects. Beasts are vast and terrible in their true forms, but I think that the idea of &quot;compulsory horror as part of your nature&quot; is already explored in far more depth elsewhere in the WoD -- and Beasts are meant to be good for crossovers, which in my mind means that they should generally avoid forcing unnecessarily heavy concepts. This doesn't mean that Beasts can't be horrific serial-killers or cannibals or whatever, but I wouldn't give them any sort of hard hunger-to-hurt-people mechanic. Mostly the main mood I'd go for is <i>melancholy</i>. Beasts are beings from another time that no longer really fit into the world. One of the main themes would be the split between accepting that and slowly fading away, or fighting against it in various ways. (Unlike, say, CtD, though, fading away wouldn't necessarily be portrayed as a horrible thing. You are still a beast. When people say that you have no place in the modern civilized world, they're not <i>entirely</i> wrong. But simply forgetting everything and having your Beast nature go into an eternal slumber wouldn't be seen as a good end-goal -- Beasts would still be trying to find a way to exist in the world on their terms.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 01-28-2017, 03:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T18:27:26-07:00","id":693237,"title":"","content":"Excellent idea. I like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T10:56:38-07:00","id":694034,"title":"","content":"Ditto. Would have fixed some the awkwardness that the ill-fit of some the pieces have and would have also avoided the whole metatheme of storytelling (that also looks like it's going to figure prominently in the Lost 2nd Ed).<br /> <br /> Nothing we can really do now but wait to see the finished product.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T03:09:32-07:00","id":701886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mp122984</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=677381#post677381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd focus on a Theme of Victimization, and a Mood of Tragic Absurdity.<br /> <br /> I would try to turn narrative into Narrative. Beasts believe that there is some outside force (perhaps even the Mother of Monsters) that drive the Horrors and Heroes to be what they are, that tries to dictate that the Horror will terrorize the populace only to be defeated by the Hero who will share his wisdom with the outside world. But the Narrative doesn't fit the real world anymore, especially not the modern one. Perhaps it never did. Teaching lessons through pain and fear without proper authority has be disapproved of for centuries, perhaps millennium. Rare is the Beast who has such authority, rarer still is the one who limits their feeding solely to the exercise of same. In stories wolves can blow in houses and eat their inhabitants as a demonstration on why work ethic is so important, but no one's going to care about work ethic if you do that in real life. The Horror doesn't care - it just wants to eat. . .</div> </div> </div> </div>I like some of the ideas you're playing with . . . but not all. As I read the text, the role of a Beast is to <i>make</i> humanity react, almost like a supernatural vaccine. And that's the problem with a Hero. The depredations of a Beast force humanity to face their problems, to get stronger, to be their own heroes. But a Hero short circuits the process - if there's some guaranteed &quot;easy&quot; solution to the problem of a Beast, humans learn nothing. They don't get stronger, they did fix the underlying issues.<br /> <br /> Way back in the 8-bit video game era, there was one called <b>Lemmings</b>. A variant on the build-a-pipeline genre, you have to get a bunch of NPCs safely through a dangerous obstacle course. The only catch is that they have no sense of self-preservation - a lemming would walk right into a fire or off a cliff. They're literally not afraid of anything (you could even turn them into suicide bombers), so had no ability to keep themselves safe. <br /> <br /> And a lot of the supernaturals of the World of Darkness would probably like to turn humanity into something similar, into nothing more than &quot;sheeple&quot;. Something you can farm for food or slaves, and which would pose no danger to their supernatural overlords. Already, a lot of them, from the Exarchs to the Seers of the Throne, are pouring a lot of resources into such a project. Humanity can't even <i>see</i> (or remember!) some of the threats.<br /> <br /> But a hunting Beast <i>forces</i> humanity to fight back, as if they knew of the danger. For example, its in the best interests of vampires to keep some slums around for easy snacking. Places where life is cheap, and the law doesn't go. But that's exactly where a Beast with a Hunger for Punishment can gorge themselves sick. And to fully sate their soul/horror, they have to go to some pretty extravagant methods. The vamps may <i>want</i> to keep the law out of the slums, but once said Beast starts sending the severed tongues of mob bosses to the President of the United States, or streaming the slow, torturous deaths of drug lords live to the world . . . watch out! There will be task forces, urban renewal committees, exposes . . . Humanity may not understand the threat, but - thanks to the Beast - they're responding <i>exactly</i> as they need to.<br /> <br /> Or for a contemporary example, look at ISIS. In the World of Darkness, there's almost certainly a Beast with a Hunger for Ruin is almost certainly involved with them - hence the reason they keep blowing up all those ancient ruins and relics. A lot of people are prepared to just ignore ISIS, since they're so far away, and fighting against equally bad people. But every time this nameless Beast blows up another ancient landmark, the rest of the world suddenly takes notice . ..<br /> <br /> So what I'd like to see (for <i>Beast</i>) are rules governing humanity's reaction to a Beast's feeding. At the low end, probably not much. But at the high end, when a Collector has a hoard of grimoires that even an archmage would envy, or a Nemesis hangs dozens of flayed corpses off the Christmas tree at Rockefeller Center . . . What are the stages of humanity's reaction, and how long does it take to force real social reform? And how much does a Hero suppress that?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T02:02:49-08:00","id":748675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/596106-fixing-beast-how-would-you-have-done-it?p=692873#post692873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I would have focused more on actually <i>being</i> a Beast. Players are actual immortal beasts out of legend who were slowly worn down by the passing of legend and diminished into humans, often forgetting what they were for large periods of time. Prosaic reality generally binds you as a human, but Beasts have the ability to force some sort of a &quot;mythic break&quot; where the world around them temporarily changes to become simpler and more storylike -- more vibrant and mythic, but with some essential part of what makes it <i>real</i> in the modern sense suppressed or removed. While this is in effect in their area, they can recall their true selves and take on their beast form.<br /> <br /> Heroes are reincarnated figures of legend. Like Beasts, they feel this yearning for a simpler mythic world, but unlike Beasts, they don't have the power to force a mythic break on the world themselves -- they can only do it when attacking Beasts. And some of them (the ones that you're likely to end up fighting, generally) find the rush of that simple black-and-white mythic world exhilarating, so they hunt Beasts in order to go back there. Heroes often see the mythic reality as more &quot;real&quot;, as if they're tearing away illusions by hunting Beasts, but the truth is more complicated -- a Beast actually <i>is</i> also a human.<br /> <br /> I would generally tone down on the moralizing aspects. Beasts are vast and terrible in their true forms, but I think that the idea of &quot;compulsory horror as part of your nature&quot; is already explored in far more depth elsewhere in the WoD -- and Beasts are meant to be good for crossovers, which in my mind means that they should generally avoid forcing unnecessarily heavy concepts. This doesn't mean that Beasts can't be horrific serial-killers or cannibals or whatever, but I wouldn't give them any sort of hard hunger-to-hurt-people mechanic. Mostly the main mood I'd go for is <i>melancholy</i>. Beasts are beings from another time that no longer really fit into the world. One of the main themes would be the split between accepting that and slowly fading away, or fighting against it in various ways. (Unlike, say, CtD, though, fading away wouldn't necessarily be portrayed as a horrible thing. You are still a beast. When people say that you have no place in the modern civilized world, they're not <i>entirely</i> wrong. But simply forgetting everything and having your Beast nature go into an eternal slumber wouldn't be seen as a good end-goal -- Beasts would still be trying to find a way to exist in the world on their terms.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That sounds amazing. I'm not sure there'd be a way to hack Beast into that form however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}